study [69–71]. The comparision table of the overpotential and Tafel slope values with the previous study shows the stage of this materil for the HER analysis (Table S1). 6.Conclusion This study presents a green and straightforward hydrothermal pro- cess for synthesizing MnFe 2O3/g-C 3N4 composites, demonstrating their potential as highly efficient electrochemical materials for energy stor- age. To assess its structural and morphological properties, the as- synthesized composite was characterized using various spectroscopic techniques, including XRD, XPS, BET, FTIR, SEM, and EDS. These ana- lyses confirmed the composite ’s well-defined structure, presence of functional groups, structural stability, high purity, and active sites. The redesigned battery-supercapacitor demonstrated high Ed and Pd while remaining stable over 12,000 cycles. The MnFe 2O3/g-C 3N4 composite has higher HER catalytic activity in alkaline conditions, as demonstrated by a much lower Tafel slope (123 mV/dec) than its individual compo - nents, implying quicker reaction kinetics. MnFe 2O3/g-C 3N4 has high promise for sophisticated supercapacitor and conversion applications. CRediT authorship contribution statement Ehtisham Umar: Writing – original draft, Software, Formal analysis, Conceptualization. Fozia Shaheen: Writing – review & editing, Super - vision. M.Waqas Iqbal: Supervision, Investigation. Atif Mossad Ali: Formal analysis, Data curation. M.A. Sayed: Visualization, Validation. Attalla F. El-kott: Formal analysis, Data curation. Eman Kashita: Validation, Software. Declaration of competing interest The authors declare that they have no known competing financial interests or personal relationships that could have appeared to influence the work reported in this paper.Acknowledgement The authors extend their appeciation to the Deanship of Research and Graduate Studies at King Khalid University for supporting this work through the grant number R.G.P. 2/128/46. The authors acknowledge the ORIC de