Molecular Catalysis 516 (2021) 111955 8low overpotentials of 0.02/0.29, 0.11/0.29 and 0.01/0.33 V for Mn- Ni3S2, Fe-Ni 3S2 and Ru-Ni 3S2, respectively, which is significantly supe- rior to the reported catalysts, especially the traditional precious-metal- based catalysts. Furthermore, by plotting 2D volcano pattern, we determined the optimal activity condition of TM-Ni 3S2 candidates, where the corresponding limiting overpotential is 0.27 V. Most impor - tantly, the OER activity origin was revealed by d-band center. Our findings may open up new opportunities and bring about new insights into the rational design of highly efficient Ni3S2-based electrocatalysts for water splitting. CRediT author statement Yibo Chen: Data curation, Investigation, Methodology, Software, Writing-Original draft. Xinyu Zhang: Formal analysis, Conceptualiza - tion, Validation, Project administration. Jiaqian Qin: Supervision, Visualization. Riping Liu: Funding acquisition, Resources, Writing- Reviewing and Editing. Declaration of Competing Interest The authors declare that they have no known competing financial interests or personal relationships that could have appeared to influence the work reported in this paper. Acknowledgments X.Y.Z acknowledges the funding support by National Natural Science Foundation of China (grant 51571174). X.Y.Z also gratefully acknowl - edge the National Science Fund for Distinguished Young Scholars for Hebei Province of China (grant E2016203376). Supplementary materials Supplementary material associated with this article can be found, in the online version, at doi:10.1016/j.mcat.2021.111955 . Reference [1]H. Sun, Z. Yan, F. Liu, W. Xu, F. Cheng, J. Chen, Self-supported transition-metal- based electrocatalysts for hydrogen and oxygen evolution, Adv. Mater. 32 (2020), 1806326 . [2]J.Y. Zhang, T.T. Wang, D.S. Xue, C. Guan, P.X. Xi, D.Q. Gao, W. Huang, Energy- level engineered hollow N-doped NiS1.03 for Zn-Air batteries, Energy Storage Mater. 25 (2020) 202–209. [3