/2 and Ag3d 3/2 orbitals of Agelemental state. Whereas, peaks with BE of 368.8 eV (Ag3d 5/2) and 374.6 eV (Ag3d 3/2) represents Ag in metallic state i.e. Ag (0). [13] These evidence strongly indicated the formation of metallic Ag(0) NPs on Ag2MoO 4 surface. For Mo 3d [Fig. 4(b)], peaks with binding energies of 235.9 eV and 232.7 eV could be assigned to 3d3/2 and 3d5/2 orbitals of Mo (VI) state, the peak separation of 3.2 eV further Fig. 2.p-XRD pattern of as-prepared (a) Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 and (b) Pt/Ag/ Ag2MoO 4; JCPDS diffraction patterns of (c) Ag2MoO 4 (d) Ag and (e) Pt respectively. Fig. 3.(a) SEM image of Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 (b) particle distribution of Ag2MoO 4 (c and d) Low- and high-resolution image of Pt/Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 (e) SAED pattern of Pt/ Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 (f, g, h and i) elemental composition of Ag/Ag 2MoO 4. A. Anjum Moinuddin et al.
