 related plot between (αhν)2 Vs energy (eV) is rep- resented in Fig. 5(b). From graph, the band gap value for Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 and Pt/Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 was calculated as 2.36 and 2.11 eV respectively. However, the major alteration in band gap value for Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 compared to other reported Ag2MoO 4 composites are due to formation of extra oxygen vacancies during photo-irradiation reduction and SPR of Ag NPs. [2,4–6] Furthermore, the reduction in band gap value of Pt/Ag/ Ag2MoO 4 indicates effective scattering of light between two metallic counterparts owing to SPR (Surface Plasmon Resonance) features. 3.5.2. FT-IR analysis The FT-IR spectra of pristine phosphomolybdic acid H3[PMo 12O40], Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 and Pt/ Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 have been represented in Fig. 5 (c). For H3[PMo 12O40], characteristics absorption peaks at 1057, 960, 877, and 770 cm␀1 corresponding to P-O stretching vibrations in PO43- tet- rahedron, asymmetric and symmetric vibrations in terminal oxygen of Mo Ot, asymmetric vibration in Mo-O b-Mo and Mo-O c-Mo bond, and bending and vibration in Mo-O e-Mo bond respectively. [17] The observed peaks represent the presence of kegging unit. However, the absence of these peaks in Ag/Ag 2MoO 4 composites has ruled out pos- sibility of Ag-PMA complex formation [18] and indicates the pure phase Fig. 4.XPS spectrum of (a) Ag 3d (b) Mo 3d (c) Pt 4f and (d) O 1 s.  A. Anjum Moinuddin et al.
