importance of reducing the size of three-dimensional MoS 2 nanosheets [70]. And also, steps and defects appeared in the MoS 2 crystal structure which can may lead to the increase of the numbers of active sites to stimulate  the catalytic activity, due to the bombardment  of argon ions during the deposition  process; Secondly,  the electron and ion conductivity  of the catalytic interface;  Lastly, the NF+CS+MoS 2 sample is superhydrophilic, it is more favorable to electrolyte to access and penetrate. All of the above factors lead to the highest electrochemical HER efficiency. Stability is another vital parameter for the evaluation of electrocatalysts. The long-term durability test of MoS 2/candle soot/Ni foam for the HER is evaluated by the chronopotentiometric testing under a constant current density of -20 ░mA░cm-2. Fig.7d compares the LSV curves of NF ░+░CS░+░MoS 2 electrode before and after durability test. The electrocatalytic activity only shows a slight decrease after 46 ░h. Remarkably, the sample shows a continuously operational stability in alkaline media over 46░h, as presented in Fig.7d. The inset of Fig.7d also shows digital photo of hydrogen evolution cell, where the generation of H 2 bubbles can be clearly seen after a total of 46 ░h. The SEM image of the sample after the stability test at constant current density of -20 ░mA░cm-2 shows that the MoS 2 nanosheets, with little change in the morphology, still grow vertically on the candle soot. TEM (Fig.S9 a-b), HAADF-EDS (Fig.S9 c) mapping images and XPS(Fig.S10) analyses also indicate no obvious changes in the crystalline structure and chemical state before and after the durability test, also suggesting the excellent durability of the sample for HER catalysts.  Furthermore, depositing electrodes with magnetron sputtering has great advantages in electrode preparation. The method is simple to operate, and all processes are completed at room temperature without auxi liary heating, which provides a new idea for the large-scale preparation of three-dimensional materials and the development of energy conversion and storage. 4 Conclusions In summary, 3D flower-like hexagonal MoS 2 composed of nanosheets with candle soot as template was prepared by magnetr on sputtering. As a result, the unique flower-like structure and the existence of metallic 1 ░T-MoS 2 significantly improve the electrochemical HER activity with larger surface area and rich defects to expose more active edge sites and shortened diffusion channels for charge transfer and separation. Particularly, a low overpotential of 56 ░mV (V vs RHE) at 10 ░mA cm -2 and a small Tafel slope of 49 ░mV decade-1 are achieved for the electrochemical HER. Furthermore, excellent long term stability in electrochemical reaction is also achieved on the NF ░+░CS░+░MoS 2 sample. The findings in the present work may open up a new avenue for design and synthesis of highly active, stable, and novel structured catalysts for electrocatalysis applications. Uncited References [71,72,73]. Acknowledgements ACCEPTED MANUSCRIPT
