nd Chemical engi- neering from Southwest Forestry University. He is now responsible for the development and synthesis of catalysts. Chenyang Xu is studying for a master ’s degree in Professor Yanhui Guo’s research group at Fudan University. He received his bachelor ’s degree in mineral processing engineering from Central South University. His current research focuses on transition metal-boron-based catalysts for hydrogen produc - tion from water electrolysis and gas transport effects. Shengpeng Chen is pursuing an M.S. degree at the Department of Materials Science, Fudan University. He obtained his B.S. degree in Electronic Science and Technology at Fudan Uni- versity. His current research focuses on the self-supported transition metal boride electrodes for water electrolysis. Prof. Dr. Yanhui Guo received his Ph.D. in School of Materials Science and Engineering, Zhejiang University in 2008. He subsequently joined the Department of Materials Science, Fudan University, as a postdoctoral fellow and became a full Professor in 2022. He also served as a visiting scholar at Department of Chemistry, University of Oxford between 2015 and 2016. He is dedicated to the research of boron-hydrogen based materials, electrolytic water hydrogen production ma- terials and technologies, solid electrolyte and solid battery technologies. J. Zhang et al.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   Nano  Energy  128 (2024  ) 109923 10"
