strate, are given in Fig. 8 a. The onset potential for hydrogen evolution reaction on all tested Pt/GC electrodes obtained by electro-chemical deposition is /C00.003 V. Potentials for the same cur- rent density of 10 mA cm /C02for Pt/GC electrodes obtained by electrochemical deposition of Pt for 30 min at deposition po-tentials of 0.20 V and 0.15 V, are /C00.063 V, and /C00.062 V, respectively. For the Pt/GC electrode obtained by the electro-chemical deposition of Pt at 0.15 V for 60 min, that potential is/C00.056 V. For Pt/GC electrode obtained by spontaneous Pt deposition on the GC, HER is hindered and starts at /C00.054 V. Fig. 8eLSV curves for: (a) Pt/GC electrodes from Fig. 7 a; and (b) corresponding Tafel plots; (c) Pt/GNPs from Fig. 7 b; and (d) corresponding Tafel plots.international journal of hydrogen energy 51 (2024) 1240 e1254 1250
