Ir, Ag and Au doped PtS 2 systems while as both methods show similar orientation for other dopants. For WS 2, it is observed that these methods predict similar orienta tion of H 2 adsorbed on the surface except for Ag and Au dopant s. Moreover, considering the adsorption energies calcu lated using PBE+D3 approach, we found that H 2 molecule stably binds over transition metal on pristine and functio nalised WS 2 with H-H bond length perpendicular to the surface. While as for PtS 2, it is observed that on Ag doped system H 2 binds over S-atom with H-H bond length parallel to the surface . For all other dopants H 2 binds over the transition metal with H-H bond length parallel to the surface in case of pris tine and Ru doped system whereas in all other cases the bond le ngth is perpendicular to the surface.  Also, when WS 2 is functionalised with Pd, the binding strength increased by an order  of magnitude and has reached to most optimum value for  HER. Conclusions In this work, we have performed DFT calculations on  two dimensional PtS 2 and WS 2 TMDCs with spin polarisation. The band structure has been obtained using hybrid HSE06 functional with spin-orbit coupling. PtS 2 is an indirect band gap semi-conductor while WS 2 displays the direct band gap. The DOS have been calculated to envisage the effect of dopant on the band gap. Further to find the optimal photocata lytic activity, we functionalize these materials with a s eries of transition metals Ru, Rh, Pd, Ag, Ir, Au, Hg. The e lectronic structure calculations for HER activity of pristine  and functionalised PtS 2 and WS 2 shows Pd doped WS 2 system shows the optimal binding energy of H 2 for HER activity among all the systems considered. Acknowledgements S.H.M. is thankful to the UGC, Government of India.  S.C, JW, R.A. would like to acknowledge Carl Tryggers Stifte lse for Vetenskaplig Forskning and Swedish Research Council . PKJ acknowledges the financial assistance from SERB, Gov t. of India. References 1 Y. Q