il in 1986 by Matsumoto and Sato 56including the Yeager and wade, Krasil shchkov, Bockris57and Hacker- man58pathway along with the renowned electrochemical oxide and oxide pathway. In basic medium, all the listed mechanismscommence with the coordination of hydroxide to the active siteas their elementary step and would proceed through di ﬀerent steps. The overpotential is higher due to kinetic barriers in eachsteps of the reaction mechanism. 58,59 OER in acidic media;(i) Electrochemical oxide path *+H 2O/*OH + H++e−(22) *OH/*O+H++e−(23) *O+H 2O/OOH *+H++e−(24) *O2/*+O 2 (25) Fig. 1 A schematic illustration of a potential HER reaction pathway on cathode.48 Fig. 2 Hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) volcano plot on metal electrodes under low pH environment. For each metal surface, the logarithm of the exchange current density j0is plotted against M –H bond energy. Reproduced with permission2Copyright 2010, American Chemical Society. 3846 |RSC Adv. ,2 0 2 3 , 13,3 8 4 3 –3876 © 2023 The Author(s). Published by the Royal Society of ChemistryRSC Advances Review Open Access Article. Published on 26 January 2023. Downloaded on 3/29/2026 3:33:19 AM. This article is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 3.0 Unported Licence. View Article Online
