A feasible preparation of leaf like 3D dendrite Mn xCd1-xS with photocatalytic hydrogen evolution Xiaowei Wang, Binghui Feng, Lei Shi* School of Petrochemical Engineering, Liaoning Petrochemical University, Fushun, 113001, China highlights graphical abstract /C15Leaf-shaped Mn xCd1-xS (LMCS) was synthesized by hydrothermal process. /C15LMCS was synthesized without the addition of template agent andsurfactant. /C15LMCS shows excellent hydrogen production rate. /C15LMCS exhibits excellent stability. article info Article history: Received 28 July 2023Received in revised form2 September 2023Accepted 10 September 2023Available online 26 September 2023 Keywords: Leaf-shaped Mn xCd1-xS Hydrogen evolutionVisible-light photocatalysisNon-template synthesisabstract It is well known that both the size and morphology of semiconductor photocatalystsimpact their performance. No template synthesis is the future trend. In this study, a seriesof Mn xCd1-xS photocatalysts with a leaf-shaped three-dimensional (3D) dendrite structure was prepared by hydrothermal method without the addition of template agent and sur- factant. The hydrogen production rate of leaf-like dendrite Mn xCd1-xS was tested under visible light irradiation with Pt as co-catalyst. The highest hydrogen production rate was1360 mmol g /C01h/C01and the highest apparent quantum yield (AQY) at 450 nm was 3.64%. In addition, the leaf-shaped Mn xCd1-xS has good cycling stability and can be used repeatedly. Finally, a reasonable reaction mechanism was proposed based on the experimental con-sequences. This work provides a feasible strategy for the construction of Mn xCd1-xS solid solutions with new morphologies. ©2023 Hydrogen Energy Publications LLC. Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved. 1. Introduction As the energy supply of the world continues to be tight, it is imperative to accelerate the transition to more green energysources [ 1,2]. Hydrogen with a high energy density, the highest caloriﬁc value and no pollution after combustion is regardedas the best substitute for fossil energy to solve the energycrisis [ 3e5]. Converting solar energy into hydrogen energy by photocatalysis technology is considered to be one of the best *Corresponding author . E-mail address: shilei@lnpu.edu.cn (L. Shi). Available online at www.sciencedirect.com ScienceDirect journal homepage: www.elsevier.com/locate/he international journal of hydrogen energy 51 (2024) 988 e997 https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2023.09.098 0360-3199/ ©2023 Hydrogen Energy Publications LLC. Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
