LMCS-2 has the strongest transient photocurrent response, the smallest electron transfer impedance and the lowest hydrogen evolution overpotential, which may be one of the reasons for the best hydrogen production performance. In order to determine the band structure of Mn xCd1-xS with leaf-shaped dendrite structure and explore the mechanism ofphotocatalytic hydrogen production, the ﬂat-band potential(E fb) of CdS, LMCS-1, LMCS-2 and LMCS-3 were tested. Mott- schottky diagram was made by combining the test data withformula C /C02¼(2/e ε0Nd)( V a-Efb-kT/e), and the value of the intersection between the tangent line and 1/C2¼0 was the ﬂat band potential (E fb) of the catalyst to be measured [ 49]. As shown in Fig. S7 , the E fbvalues (vs. Ag/AgCl) of CdS, LMCS-1, LMCS-2 and LMCS-3 are /C01.09 eV, /C01.55 eV, /C01.62 eV and /C01.72 eV, respectively. With the increase of Mn content, the ﬂat band potential becomes more and more negative, indi-cating that the reduction ability of the catalyst is stronger andstronger, and the hydrogen evolution ability is enhanced [50].The tangent line of Mott-Schottky curve shows a positiveslope, then CdS, LMCS-1, LMCS-2 and LMCS-3 are n-typesemiconductors [ 38], then E fbis 0.1eV more correct than E CB, and the relationship between E CBand E fbin n-type semi- conductors satisﬁes the formula E CB(vs. NHE) ¼Efb(vs. Ag/ AgCl) þEq-0.1eV [ [ 38], 51]. According to the relationship be- tween E CB,EVBand Eg ¼EVB-ECB, the valence band potential (EVB) of CdS can be known. The band structure of CdS, LMCS-1,LMCS-2 and LMCS-3 is shown in Fig. 9 . According to the E CB position, Mn xCd1-xS has strong reducing capacity to promote water cracking to produce hydrogen. According to the band structure of Mn xCd1-xS, the possible photocatalytic hydrogen evolution mechanism is proposed asfollows ( Fig. 10 ): When the light gives a certain energy, the photogenerated electrons (e /C0) and holes (hþ) in LMCS-2 are separated, and the electrons and holes move to the surface ofthe catalyst. At this time, the sacriﬁcants SO 32/C0and S2/C0 Fig. 8 e(a) Transient photocurrent response curves, (b) EIS-Nyquist plots, (c) PL spectra (380 nm), and (d) LSV plots of the prepared samples (a:CdS, b:LMCS-1, c:LMCS-2, d:LMCS-3). Fig. 9 eElectronic band structure of CdS, LMCS-1, LMCS-2 and LMCS-3.international journal of hydrogen energy 51 (2024) 988 e997 994
