consume most of the hþand transform into S 2O32/C0and SO 42/C0 [51], and e/C0is transferred to the surface of Pt to participate in the hydrogen evolution reaction. The photogenerated e/C0and hþare effectively separated. 4. Conclusion In this work, a leaf petal dendrite-structured Mn xCd1-xS pho- tocatalyst was prepared for the ﬁrst time by a simple hydro- thermal method without adding any templating agent or surfactant. This synthesis method can avoid the high costcaused by the use of template agent and the operation issimple, which accords with the concept of green chemistry.The blade structure provides more Pt particle acceptance sitesand more active sites for photocatalytic hydrogen production.The leaf petal dendrite-structured Mn xCd1-xS showed excel- lent photocatalytic HER activity in a sacriﬁcial solution loadedwith 1.5 wt% Pt. The largest speciﬁc surface area, the strongestphotogenerated carrier separation ability, the smallest elec-tron transfer resistance and the most negative hydrogen precipitation overpotential make LMCS-2 exhibit the best hydrogen evolution ability. The HER of LMCS-2 reaches 1360mmolg /C01h/C01, which is three times higher than that of CdS, and the AQY at 450 nm reaches 3.64%. This work provides afeasible strategy for constructing Mn xCd1-xS solid solutions with new morphologies for photocatalytic hydrogen evolutionapplications. Declaration of competing interest The authors declare that they have no known competingﬁnancial interests or personal relationships that could haveappeared to inﬂuence the work reported in this paper.Acknowledgements We acknowledge the ﬁnancial supported from talent scientiﬁcresearch fund of LSHU (2016XJJ-080) and basic scientiﬁc research project of Liaoning Provincial Department of Educa- tion (L2023008). Appendix A. Supplementary data Supplementary data to this article can be found online athttps://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2023.09.098 . references [1]Pakulska T. Green energy in central and eastern European (CEE) countries: new challenges on the path to sustainabledevelopment. Energies 2021;14(4):884 . [2]Borowski P, Karlikowska B. Clean hydrogen is a challenge for enterprises in the era of low-emission and zero-emissioneconomy. Energies 2023;16(3):1171 . [3]Jiang Y, Toe CY, Mofarah SS, Cazorla C, Chang S, Yin Y, Zhang Q, Lim S, Yao Y, Tian R, Wang Y, Zaman T, Arandiyan H, Andersson G, Scott J, Koshy P, Wang D, Sorrell C. Efﬁcientcocatalyst-free piezo-photocatalytic hydrogen evolution of defective BaTiO3 ex nanoparticles from seawater. ACS Sustainable Chem Eng 2023;11(8):3370 e89. [4]Zhao X, Feng J, Liu J, Lu J, Shi W, Yang G, Wang G, Feng P, Cheng P. Metal-Organic framework-derived ZnO/ZnS heteronanostructures for efﬁcient visible-light-driven photocatalytic hydrogen production. Adv Sci2018;5(4):1700590 . [5]Yu L, Li X, Duan L, Zhang Y, Zhu H. Oxygen vacancies- induced dendritic SrTiO3/CdS p en heterostructures photocatalyst for ultrahigh hydrogen evolution. Sol RRL2023;7(14):2300259 . Fig. 10 eSchematic diagram of foliated dendrite Mn xCd1-xS photocatalytic hydrogen production mechanism.international journal of hydrogen energy 51 (2024) 988 e997 995
