Article A general approach to high-entropy metallic nanowire electrocatalysts A reduction-diffusion strategy for making a library of Pt-based high-entropy alloy nanowires (HEA NWs) with atomic thickness and up to ten components (Pt, Mo, Rh,Ir, Ru, Co, Ni, Fe, Mn, and Cr) at low temperatures is reported. This general methodcan be used to synthesize 26 kinds of multimetallic NWs, including 17 HEAs. The severe lattice distortion in HEA NWs alters the strain distribution, leading to the tunable electronic structure for enhanced energy electrocatalysis. Yingjun Sun, Wenshu Zhang, Qinghua Zhang, Yingjie Li, LinGu, Shaojun Guo guosj@pku.edu.cn Highlights A general approach for atomic- thick high-entropy alloy (HEA) nanowires (NWs) Revealing the reduction-diffusion mechanism of HEA NWsformation HEA NWs achieve superior catalytic activities for HOR/HER Sun et al., Matter 6, 193–205 January 4, 2023 ª2022 Elsevier Inc. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.matt.2022.09.023 ll
