To evaluate the anti-CO poisoning ability of 5-HEA NWs, we further examined the HOR activities of HEA NWs in the presence of 1,000 ppm CO ( Figures 5 Ea n d S36). The 5-HEA NWs/C shows the smallest de crease of 3.7% in the limiting current density compared with other prepared catalysts, indicating excellent selectivity forHOR against CO. The stability of catalysts was evaluated using chronoamperometry(CA) at 0.1 V in the presence of 1,000 ppm CO to further verify the resistance of HEA NWs to CO ( Figure 5 F). It can be noted that the activity of 5-HEA NWs catalyst decreased by only 18.9% after continuous operation for 2,000 s. In contrast,3-PtRuMo NWs and PtRu/C lost 95.7% and 61.3% of their activity under the sameconditions, respectively, and the Pt/C was completely inactivated after 1,850 s test. We also demonstrated the denary Pt 18Rh16Mo 15Ir11Co9Ru6Fe6Mn 5Cr5HEA NWs (10-HEA NWs) as an efﬁcient catalyst to boost HER performance ( Figure S37 ). Figure 5. Structural characterization and HOR measurements of 5-PtRhMoRuIr HEA NWs (A and B) HAADF-STEM image (A) and STEM mapping (B) of 5-HEA NWs.(C) HOR polarization curves of 5-HEA NWs/C, 3-PtRuMo NWs/C, commercial PtRu/C, andcommercial Pt/C catalysts in H 2-saturated 0.1 M KOH with a scan rate of 5 mV s/C01at the rotating speed of 1,600 rpm. (D) Exchange current densities (left) and kinetic current densities (right, at 50 mV) normalized bymetal mass. (E) HOR polarization curves of 5-HEA NWs/C in pure H 2or 1,000 ppm CO/H 2-saturated 0.1 M KOH. (F) Relative current-time chronoamperometry response of different catalysts in 1,000 ppm CO/H 2- saturated 0.1M KOH at 0.1 V versus RHE.ll 200 Matter 6, 193–205, January 4, 2023Article
