10-HEA NWs display the lowes t overpotential of 24 mV at a current density of 10 mA cm/C02 geo,f a rs u p e r i o rt o3 - P t 45Rh43Mo 12NWs (66 mV) and commercial Pt/C. At /C00.05 V versus RHE, the 10-HEA NWs show the highest mass activities of 6 A mg/C01 Pt, /C248.6 times higher than that of 3-NWs. Remarkably, the 10-HEA NWs catalyst also has better durability than those of 3-NWs and Pt/C. All electrochemical results demonstrate that the reduction-diffusion method is a general route to designing HEA catalysts with high activity and excellent durability. Conclusion In summary, we demonstrate a general reduction-diffusion, low-temperature strat- egy for creating a library of Pt-based HEA NW single-phase solid solutions with upto ten components. We found that tuning/controlling the reduction and diffusionrate of various atoms on preformed Pt NWs is the key to obtaining Pt-based HEA NWs, of which CO molecules cannot only control the direction of crystal growth by adsorbing on speciﬁc crystal pla nes, but also inhibit the elemental sep- aration and phase segregation. Using th is reduction-diffusion wet-chemistry method, we extend to synthesize Pt-based multi-metal alloy NWs containing 17kinds of HEAs. We demonstrate that compared with LEA, Pt-based HEA NWsshow obvious lattice distortion, which can regulate and tune strain distributionand electronic structure, thus leading to outstanding HOR/HER catalytic perfor- mance. This work aims to provide a new general method for fabricating Pt-based HEAs with tailored structures at low temperatures for energy electrocatalysis and other potential reactions. EXPERIMENTAL PROCEDURES Resource availability Lead contact Further information and requests for resou rces and reagents should be directed to and will be fulﬁlled by the lead contact, Shaojun Guo, guosj@pku.edu.cn . Materials availability This study did not generate new unique reagents. Data and code availability All experimental data and source code supporting the ﬁndings of 