help promote Pt eHadsinteractions at the neighbouring sites and energetically favour H 2generation [ 65,66]. Electrochemical measurements for hydrogen evolution reaction The HER performance of the hierarchical-architecture PtFeRhRu nanoalloy was investigated in 1.0 M KOH acting as the electrolyte (see supporting information for details), andthe results obtained were compared with those obtained usingthe hierarchical-architecture PtFeRh (Pt: Fe: Rh ¼0.763: 0.179: 0.058; Fig. S3a and Figs. S4a ec), PtFeRu (Pt: Fe: Ru ¼0.794: 0.173: 0.033; Fig. S3b and Figs. S4d ef) and PtFe (Pt: Fe ¼0.826: 0.174; Fig. S3c ,Figs. S4g ei) nanoalloys as well as commercial Pt/C. The electrochemically active surface area (ECSA) of thedendritic PtFeRhRu nanoalloys, PtFeRh nanoalloys, PtFeRu nanoalloys, PtFe nanoalloys and Pt/C was evaluated in 0.1 MHClO 4solution ( Fig. S5 )/by CO stripping in 0.1 M HClO 4solu- tion ( Fig. S6 ), the ECSA of them is respectively 42.7/39.6, 41.3/ 37.5, 25.1/20.4, 28.6/23.3 and 69.2/65.2 m2gPt/C01). Among them, the PtFeRhRu nanoalloy exhibited the highest electrocatalyticactivity ( Fig. 4 aec). The overpotential at a current density of 10 mA cm /C02for the PtFeRhRu nanoalloy was 20.0 mV, whereas the corresponding parameters for the PtFeRh nanoalloy, the PtFeRu alloy, the PtFe alloy and Pt/C were 31.0, 41.0, 61.0 and 80.0 mV, respectively, indicating that the simultaneousintroduction of Fe, Rh and Ru into Pt can considerably promotethe activity of the catalyst. The current density normalised bythe electrode geometric area ( Fig. S7 ) of the PtFeRhRu nano- alloy at /C00.05,/C00.07 and /C00.1 V @ RHE became 41.27, 64.64 and Fig. 1 e(a) SEM images of the hierarchical-architecture dendritic PtFeRhRu nanoalloys. (b) XRD spectra of the hierarchical- architecture dendritic PtFeRhRu nanoalloys. (c) HAADF-STEM image of the dendritic PtFeRhRu nanoalloys. (d) Cross-sectional compositional line proﬁles of the dendritic PtFeRhRu nanoalloys. (e ei) EDX element mappings of the dendritic PtFeRhRu nanoalloys.international journal of hydrogen energy 46 (2021) 11573 e11586 11576
