15 The TOF of NiFe 2O4/CB and Exf NiFe 2O4/CB electrocatalysts at ŋ = 187 mV was 0.0017 and 1 0.077 s -1, respectively. The TOF of Exf NiFe 2O4/CB is more than four times higher than that of 2 NiFe 2O4/CB, which presenting the higher activity on Exf Ni Fe 2O4/CB.  3 The Electrochemical kinetics were then studied usin g Tafel plots to provide an adequate 4 description of the kinetics of the HER as displayed  in Figure 8 . The Tafel slope mainly depends 5 on the excess active sites within the surface of th e catalyst and also the conductivity that enables 6 an effective transfer of charges [7, 8, 68]. By fit ting the linear regions (extracted from the Tafel 7 plots) into the Tafel equation, (7) the Tafel slope s can be determined.  8 ŋ = b log ( j) +  a                                      (7) 9 Where: ŋ is the overpotential, j the electrode’s current density, a is a constant and b is the Tafel slope.  10 The Tafel slopes of NiFe 2O4/CB, Exf-NiFe 2O4/CB and Pt/C electrocatalysts derived from the 11 polarization plots are shown in Fig. 8(b).  The Tafel slope of 30 mV dec -1, 40 mV dec -1  and 120 mV 12 dec -1  should be observed if either the Tafel, Heyrovsky or Volmer reaction is the rate determining 13 step, respectively [69,70]. The Exf-NiFe 2O4/CB material possessed a Tafel slope of 85.8 mV dec-1 14 which falls between the Heyrovsky mechanism (40 mV dec -1) and the Volmer mechanism (120 mV 15 dec -1) at a rate determining step. Thus, the Exf-NiFe 2O4/CB electrocatalyst should probably follow a 16 Volmer-Heyrovsky mechanism, where both reactions af fect the HER [69,71].  17 The NiFe 2O4/CB electrocatalyst with a Tafel slope of 122.7 mV dec -1, can be assigned to the 18 Volmer reaction mechanism. As a reference material,  Pt/C electrocatalyst shows the Tafel slope 19 of 28 mV dec -1 due to its high adsorbed hydrogen coverage. This pr oposes that the HER on Pt/C 20 electrocatalyst proceeds a reaction with the Tafel rate-determining step [71]. From the above 21 results, It further indicated that HER reaction mec hanism on the Exf-NiFe 2O4/CB electrocatalyst 22 have been changed compared to NiFe 2O4/CB electrocatalyst.   23 High durability is another imperative property as a  reliable electrocatalyst. To evaluate the 24 durability, the electrochemical stability of the Ex f-NiFe 2O4/CB electrocatalyst was tested by 25 cyclic voltammetry (CV) between 0 and -1.2 V (vs RH E) at 200 mV s -1 in 0.5 M H 2SO 4 for 26
