17 de-aggregation/de-agglomeration of the particles. O n the other hand, through the formation of 1 the ultrasonic cavitation, the radials from water a re generated and relieved quickly.  2 Table 3.  Electrochemical performance of various electrocata lysts for HER in acidic media. 3 Catalysts ŋ10 , mV     Tafel slope (mV dec -1) ŋ10* , mV (cycles No) electrolyte H2SO 4 (M) Refs CP@Ni-P   98      58.8    150 (10 3) 0.5 [72] MoS 2/RGO 150   41    160 (10 3) 0.5 [73] CoSe 2 MP/CC 193   50    213 (10 3) 0.5 [74] C3N4@NG 240      51.5 ~260 (10 3) 0.5 [75] CoNi@NC         142 104 ~200 (10 3) 0.1 [76] Exf-NiFe 2O4/CB 187      85.8       123 (6x10 3) 0.5 This work ŋ10  overpotential at 10 mA cm -2; ŋ10*  overpotential at 10 mA cm -2 after stability test. 4 Meanwhile, the temperature in the cavitation exceed s 1000 ºC, causing the surface modification, 5 elemental ion enrichment and embedding/interchange of metal ions within the surface layer of 6 the NiFe 2O4/CB nanospheres [31,77], as identified from the TEM , XRD, FTIR and XPS results. 7 The XPS analysis indicated ultrasonication boosts t he formation of oxygen vacancies on the 8 surface that perhaps improve the conductivity of th e NiFe 2O4/CB. Additionally, the more Fe 3+  9 and Ni 2+  cation occupy A sites instead of B cites after exf oliation, which enhance the stability of 10 structure of  NiFe 2O4 since B site cations are less stable than A site c ations. The XRD analysis 11 of the catalysts after the stability test is displa yed in Fig. S2 . The carbon peaks appeared 12 significantly after 6000 cycles and the crystallite  of the Exf-NiFe 2O4/CB was improved based on 13 the increase of the intensity of the peaks, indicat ing an increased conductivity and stabilized 14 structure of the NiFe 2O4/CB  with increasing cycles. Moreover, the high-intensit y ultrasound 15 exfoliation induced the corrosion stability due to the formation of  hydrophilic surfaces on 16 NiFe 2O4/CB nanospheres [78]. Norskov and Henkelman have ex plored the strain and ligand 17 effects on electrochemical bimetallic catalysts [79 -81]. In this work, from the XRD results of 18 NiFe 2O4 and Exf NiFe 2O4, it was observed that the crystal structure and th e lattice constants of 19 NiFe 2O4 does not change after exfoliation, indicating that the strain effect can be ignored on the 20
============================================================
[Page 21/30]
