Journal Name  ARTICLE This journal is © The Royal Society of Chemistry 20 xx  J. Name ., 2013, 00 , 1-3 | 9 Please do not adjust margins Please do not adjust margins Fig. 5 Changes in transfer characteristics of graph ene field effect transistors (FETs) in response to porphyrin adsorption and metalation on graphene: (a) 2H-TPyP adsorption on g raphene-1 (G1), -2 (G2), and -3 (G3) and voltage-ap plied metalation to Ni-TPyP, Zn-TPyP, and Pt-TPyP, respectively, (b) 2H -TAPP adsorption on graphene-4 (G4), -5 (G5), and - 6 (G6) and voltage- applied metalation to Ni-TAPP, Zn-TAPP, and Pt-TAPP , respectively, (c) 2H-TPP adsorption on graphene-7  (G7), -8 (G8), and -9 (G9) and voltage-applied metalation to Ni-TPP, Zn-T PP, and Pt-TPP, respectively. (d) Illustrations sho wing interfaces of 2H- TPyP/graphene and M-TPyP/graphene based on the rela tive electronegativity of atoms. Based on the adsorption of 2H-TPyP and 2H-TAPP, inf luence of intermolecular hydrogen bonding (involving water molecules) on transfer characteristics of graphene was evident. With regard to the adsorption of 2H-TPyP, the lone- pair electrons of pyridine groups at meso -positions did not participate in the π-system, while the lone-pair electrons of the central N 4 sites contributed to the π-system, making pyridine groups a weak base and allowing the format ion of hydrogen bonds with water molecules. 55-56  Intermolecular hydrogen bonding via  water molecules between the protonated pyridine substitutes of the neighbouring  porphyrins induced electron transfer from graphene to the 2H- TPyP layer, indicating electropositive doping, and charge neutrality points shifted in the positive direction . Even though the 2H-TPyP/graphene samples were thoroughly dried under vacuum at 80 °C for several days, water molecules t rapped by intermolecular hydrogen bonding were confined betwe en pyridine terminals in the 2H-TPyP layer. However, w hen the applied temperature was high enough ( i.e ., 250 °C) to disturb (or destroy) the intermolecular hydrogen bonding, t he electropositive doping effects were significantly r educed (Fig. S8a in the ESI). The adsorbed 2H-TAPP molecules, wh ich have Page 9 of 12 Nanoscale Nanoscale Accepted Manuscript Published on 23 February 2017. Downloaded by University of Newcastle on 26/02/2017 19:36:11. View Article Online DOI: 10.1039/C6NR09428G
