o 2S3 synthesised samples. The XPS analysis was further conducted to study the oxidation states Fig. 1.XRD results of (a) Mo2S3; (b) SnO 2-Co3O4, and (c) SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3; XPS results of SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite (d) survey scan with the inset having elemental atomic percentages; elemental scan results of (e) Co 2p; (f) Mo 3d; (g) S 2p; (h) O 1 s, and (i) Sn 3d; FESEM images of (j, k) coral-shaped Mo2S3 nano- flowers; (l, m) SnO 2-Co3O4 nanocubes, and (n-p) SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite (rescaled-enlarged representations of the individual scale bars have been provided for clear visualization).P. Chaubey et al.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Surfaces  and Interfaces  72 (2025)  107099 4
