. Similarly, the calculated Jo value of 0.71 mA/cm2 for the synthesised SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite is least compared to Mo2S3 (0.87 mA/cm2), and SnO 2-Co3O4 nanocubes (1.43 mA/cm2). This lowest Jo value of SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nano- composite compared to other samples, further signifies the optimised internal HER kinetic applicability of this nanocomposite. Additionally, a comparative analysis of the J₀ values with the previously reported electrocatalysts in the literature has been provided in Table ST1 of the supplementary information, which further establishes the superior HER performance of our SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite with respect to the other reported materials. Furthermore, HER kinetics are examined from the Tafel slope anal- ysis and is shown in Fig. 4(f). Pristine Mo2S3 and SnO 2-Co3O4 exhibited the Tafel slopes of 259.07 mV/dec and 233.31 mV/dec, respectively, whereas, SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite show significantly reduced Tafel slope of 102.8 mV/dec. This implies the slower reaction kinetics of pristine Mo2S3 and SnO 2-Co3O4 as compared to the significantly Fig. 4.CV plots of (a) Mo2S3; (b) SnO 2-Co3O4; (c) SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite; (d) Δj vs. scan rate plot; (e) HER polarisation plots; (f) HER Tafel plot; (g) comparative bar plot of HER overpotential and Tafel slope values for Mo2S3, SnO 2-Co3O4 and, SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite; (h) CA measurement of SnO 2- Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite over a period of 24-hours; (i) HER polarisation curve before and after 24-hours stability analysis of SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite.P. Chaubey et al.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                Surfaces  and Interfaces  72 (2025)  107099 8
