bes and Mo2S3 coral-shaped nanoflowers. In OER, 192.3 mV overpotential value at 10 mA/cm2 current density was ob- tained with a reduced Tafel slope of 99 mV/dec, which is comparable and frequently far ahead of numerous cutting-edge electrocatalysts. The material exhibits good electrocatalytic properties in HER as well, achieving a Tafel slope of 102.8 mV/dec and an overpotential of 204.98 mV at 10 mA/cm2. This synthesised SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite surpassed the 24-hours of stability testing in both HER and OER. Only 1.45 V cell voltage at 10 mA/cm2 current density is needed when using SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite as both the cathode and anode in a two-electrode system in 2.0 M KOH alkaline solution for OWS. Also, a 72-hours of exceptional stability testing for OWS was successfully ach- ieved. Outstanding electrocatalytic performance was obtained by this synthesised SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite. The superior electro - catalytic efficiency of this multi-interfacial SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 hetero - structural assembly was due to the following results (a) multiple interfaces formed among SnO 2, Co3O4, and Mo2S3 accelerated the electron transfer movements which ultimately boosted the OER and HER bifunctional processes. (b) The synergistic interactions among SnO 2, Co3O4, and Mo2S3 phases further optimized the electronic configura - tions for accelerating the adsorption of various intermediate species. (c) The enhanced electrocatalytic active surface area and number of active redox sites have further improved the electrocatalytic efficiency of the SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite. These improved characteristics of the SnO 2-Co3O4-Mo 2S3 nanocomposite open the door for its possible use in electrochemical water splitting devices, metal-air batteries, fuel cells, and industrial based applications in the future. Declaration of generative AI and AI-assisted technologies in the writing process During the preparation of this work, the author(s) used Grammerly-a writing