RESEARCH ARTICLE www.afm-journal.de AMulti-SiteSynergisticEﬀectinHigh-EntropyAlloyfor EﬃcientHydrogenEvolution YiWan,WenruiWei,ShengqiDing,LiangWu,HaiyingQin,andXianxiaYuan* Unravelingthemechanismdrivenbyelectronegativity-dominatedelectronic conﬁgurationiscrucialfordevelopinghigh-entropyalloysaseﬃcientcatalyst forhydrogenevolutionreaction(HER).Inthiswork,diﬀerentatomswith diverseelectronegativitiesareexploredtoregulatetheelectrocatalyticactivity ofPtFeCoNi@HCStowardHER,resultinginPtFeCoNiCuCr@HCSwithan overpotentialof29mVat10mAcm−2andenhanceddurabilitysurpassing thatofcommercial20%Pt/CinKOHenvironment.Basedonvarious physicochemicalandelectrochemicaltechniquesaswellasdensityfunctional theorycalculations,amulti-sitesynergisticeﬀectwithinPtFeCoNiCuCr@HCS materialiselucidatedintermsofbothstructuralcompositionand electrocatalyticprocess.Brieﬂy,PtandCuserveasthefundamentalelements toformface-centeredcubiccrystalframework,Crprimarilyfunctionsasan electrondonortoregulatetheelectronicconﬁguration,Coservesasthemain activesiteforwaterdissociation,andtheproducedhydrogenspeciespreferto transfertowardPt,Fe,andCusitesforhydrogenformation.Thisworkoﬀers anin-depthinsightonthesynergisticmechanisminhighentropyalloysandis helpfulfordesigningeﬃcientelectrocatalysts. 1.Introduction Global energy crises and environmental concerns drive the in- creasing demand for sustainable and clean energy.[1]Hydrogen energyisoneofthemostpromisingcandidatesduetotheadvan- tageofhighenergydensityandabundantsource,makingitsuit- ableforwidespreadapplicationintheﬁeldsoftransportationand industrialproduction.Inrecentyears,electrocatalyticwatersplit- tinghasgainedgreatattentionasanelectrochemicalenergycon- version technology enabling eﬃcient hydrogen production.[2–4] Herein, the kinetics of hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) sig- niﬁcantlyaﬀecttheeﬃciencyofoverallwatersplitting,[5]andthe Y.Wan,W.Wei,S.Ding,L.Wu,X.Yuan SchoolofChemistryandChemicalEngineering ShanghaiJiaoTongUniversity Shanghai200240,China E-mail:yuanxx@sjtu.edu.cn H.Qin NewEnergyMaterialsResearchCenter CollegeofMaterialsandEnvironmentalEngineering HangzhouDianziUniversity Hangzhou310018,China TheORCIDidentiﬁcationnumber(s)fortheauthor(s)ofthisarticle canbefoundunder https://doi.org/10.1002/adfm.202414554 DOI:10.1002/adfm.202414554development of eﬃcient and durable elec- trocatalysts to accelerate the HER process is of great vital.[6]Noble metal catalysts, such as Pt, possess superior capability to- wardHER,buttheirlarge-scaleapplication ishinderedbythehighcostandlimitedre- sources.Inthiscase,alloyingrepresentsan eﬀective strategy to reduce the consump- tion of noble metals while simultaneously enhancing the electrocatalytic activity.[7,8] High entropy alloys (HEAs) are a type of materials with a multi-element struc- ture that emerged recently,[9]and the sim- ilar atomic radius or low mixing enthalpy is crucial in their formation, as it en- ables a homogeneous solid solution struc- turetoavoidphaseseparation.[10]Many re- searcheshavedemonstratedsuccessfulfab- rication of HEAs with stable and homo- geneous structure using noble (Pt, Ru, Ir, etc.) or transition metals (Fe, Co, Ni, Cu, etc.),[11,12]and the resulting unique archi- tectureoﬀersseveraladvantagesonelectro- catalytic capability compared to traditional catalysts: 1) It allows for eﬀective regulation of microstructure and electron distribution to optimize the adsorption energy be- tween hydrogen intermediates and active sites, resulting in im- proved kinetics for hydrogen evolution;[13]2) The high mixing entropycausessluggishdiﬀusionoftheatomswithinthestruc- ture, eﬀectively preventing degradation and corrosion of HEA materials.[14]Theseintrinsicfeaturesensureagoodactivityand durability of HEA materials under harsh conditions, making them a type of promising catalyst widely applicated in electro- catalyticwatersplitting. Moreover,itappearstobeaneﬀectiveandviablestrategyforac- celeratingHERkineticsthroughtheincorporationofatomswith disparateelectronegativitiesintohighentropysystem,[15]andthe stability of HEAs is directly linked to the interactions between the elements which are reﬂected in their electronegativities,[16] as electronegativity represents the varying electron-attracting or -donatingabilitiesofdiﬀerentatoms.Therefore,appropriateelec- tronegativity enables eﬀective optimization of local electronic conﬁguration,therebyfacilitatingtheadsorption/desorptionpro- cess of intermediates during the HER process and enhancing the stability.[17]For example, Zhu et al. compared the eﬀects of incorporating Cr, Mn, and Cu with diﬀerent electronegativi- tiesonelectrocatalyticperformanceofthehighentropymaterial of FeCoNiRu/CNF as HER catalyst,[15]and revealed that Mn is moresuitablethanbothCrandCuforregulatingtheelectronic Adv. Funct. Mater. 2025,35,2414554 ©2024Wiley-VCHGmbH 2414554(1of11)
