www.advenergymat.de www.advancedsciencenews.com© 2018 WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim 1800575 (2 of 7) large particle dimension, which would in turn limit their cata- lytic performances. Therefore, it is urgent to explore and design desired vanadium carbide electrocatalysts, which possess com- parable or even better catalytic performance than Pt. In this work, inspired by pioneers’ studies, we designedly fabricated single crystal platinum-like V 8C7 electrocatalysts. In contrast with the ordinary vanadium carbide, the nonstoichi- ometry V 8C7 is virtually filled while 12.5% of carbon sites are vacant. In and around the defect of carbon sites, superfluous electrons are delocalized among the neighboring V atoms and the electron enriched carbon vacancy serves as an active center for HER. [13] In 1981, Oshima et al. proved that the surface prop- erties of platinum-like TMCs largely depend on their single-crystalline surfaces. [14] Hence, we have reason to believe that the single-crystal platinum-like V 8C7 exposed with the highly active facet would possess outstanding HER activity. For this purpose, three innovative tactics were employed to designedly fabricate our target material. First, for obtaining single-crystalline V 8C7 at the high synthetic temperature, we adopt graphited-carbon shells as a maskant to cut down the growth rate of V 8C7 crystals utilizing the confinement effect of carbon shells.[15] Afterward, density functional theory (DFT) computations were carried out to determine the crystal faces with highly HER activity. Fol- lowing that, V 8C7 with highly active facet was converted from vanadium oxide based on a low crystal-mismatch strategy. Broadly speaking, the graphited-carbon enveloped platinum- like V 8C7 nanosheets on nickel foam (noted as V 8C7@GC NSs/ NF ) with high-activity facet exposed, should deliver excellent electroconductivity and ample active-sites in improving the HER performance. The schematic diagram of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF is demon- strated in Figure 1a. First, the NH 4VO 3 NSs/NF is coated with layers of glucose polymer via the hydrogen-bonding actions between glucose and ammonia ions (see Figure S1, Sup- porting Information).[16,17] Under the protecting of carbon films, the NH 4VO 3 NSs/NF is converted into interweaved VO@GC NSs/NF, which is subsequently reduced by CH 4 to form single-crystalline V 8C7@GC NSs. For exploring the for - mation mechanism of single crystal interweaved V 8C7@GC NSs, series of contrast experiments are carried out at the same time. Obviously, the carbon coating plays a key role in reducing the crystalline growth velocity of VO and V 8C7 crystals, which eventually generates hierarchically single crystal V 8C7@GC NSs/NF (Figure S2, Supporting Information).[18] Proverbially, graphited carbon delivers negligible catalytic activity toward HER. As a result, it is significant to reduce the carbon coating thickness without any structure collapse of V 8C7@GC NSs/ NF. Furthermore, CH 4 atmosphere is decisive to the formation of V 8C7, without which only interweaved V 2O3@GC NSs/NF could be obtained at the same condition (Figure S3, Supporting Adv. Energy Mater. 2018, 1800575 Figure 1. a) The fabrication process of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF, b) low- and high-magnification FE-SEM images of b,e) NH 4VO 3 NSs/NF, c,f) VO@GC NSs/NF, and d,g) V 8C7@GC NSs/NF, respectively.
