www.advenergymat.de www.advancedsciencenews.com© 2018 WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim 1800575 (4 of 7) facet is 0.11 eV, which is even in close proximity to that of Pt (around 0.09 eV). The smaller |∆G H*| of V 8C7 compared to that of VC (0.191 eV) indicates that V 8C7 possesses better intrinsic catalytical activity contributing to the existence of carbon vacan-cies (Table S3, Supporting Information). Above all, on account of the synergistic effects between metallic platinum-like V 8C7 networks, double-deck carbon layers coating and highly active (110) facet exposed, V 8C7@GC NSs/NF should present remark- ably catalytic activity toward HER comparable to that of Pt. In order to dissect the reaction process and verify the exposed crystal face of single-crystal interweaved V 8C7@GC NSs, the transmission electron microscopy (TEM) and high-resolution (HR) TEM tests are conducted. Figure 3a,d indicates the typically single crystal nanosheet feature of NH 4VO 3 precursor. Besides, Figure 3b,c verifies that interweaved VO@GC and V 8C7@ GC networks are made of crossed nanorods. The TEM images focused at the crossed nanorod junction indicate that each V 8C7 nanorod elongates the equivalent growth direction (Figure S10, Supporting Information). Following that, the crystalline struc- ture of separated V 8C7 nanorods in the interleave networks is characterized by selected area electron diffraction (SAED), which delivers orderly arranged spots with a tetragonal sym- metry, manifesting that the interleave nanorods possess high crystallinity and single crystal feature (Figure 3c).The HRTEM image and Raman spectrum of carbon shell confirm the exist- ence of graphitized carbon, providing fast electron transport, and improved electrical contact with the active sites (Figure S11, Supporting Information). As shown in Figure 3e, two sets of well-resolved crystal lattice interdistances are determined to be 0.29 and 0.41 nm, respectively, indexed to the (110) and (001) crystal planes of cubic VO phase. It is obvious in Figure 3f that the clear lattice fringes with interplanar spacings of 0.29 and 0.42 nm are associated with the (220) and (002) planes of cubic V8C7 phase. Interestingly, the crystal mismatch between VO and V 8C7 is below 4% from the calculation based on the crystal planes of (220), (002) in V 8C7 and (110), (001) in VO.[21] The small crystal mismatch indicates a minimal reorganization of structure in the transformation process, which is the key to form single-crystalline cubic V 8C7 from a single-crystalline cubic VO. Therefore, based on the above-mentioned discussions, it is evi- dential to conclude that the carbon maskant and low crystal mis- match are the two key factors for the formation of single crystal interweaved V 8C7@GC networks. What is more, by indexing the crystal lattices and fast Fourier transform (FFT) pattern, the exposed plane of V 8C7 networks is identified as (110). As a result, (110) facet with highly catalytic activity was successfully obtained without the need to conquer large energy gap. After forecasting the excellent HER performances of V 8C7@ GC NSs/NF by theoretical simulation, we assess the HER per - formances of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF over wide pH range. Com- mercial Pt sheet, V 8C7 NSs/NF, and blank NF with the same geometrical surface area are adopted as references. As seen in Figure 4a–c, the NF delivers ignorable HER activity in all elec- trolytes, indicating that the activity is mainly derived from the V 8C7@GC rather than substrate. As proved by the linear sweep voltammetry (LSV) curves in Figure 4a, Pt exhibits expect- antly catalytic activity in alkaline electrolyte. The overpotential of Pt for achieving the current density of −10 mA cm−2 (η 10) is 49 mV, followed by V 8C7 NSs/NF (62 mV), while the η10 of V8C7@GC NSs/NF is as low as 47 mV. As summarized in Table S4 (Supporting Information), V 8C7@GC NSs/NF possesses the lowest η10 in all pH-universal HER catalysts reported in the alkaline media so far, e.g., Mo 2C@NC (60 mV),[22] Mn-Co-P/ Ti (108 mV),[23] CoP/CC (209 mV),[24] Ni 1−xCoxSe2 MNSN/NF (85 mV),[25] and Zn 0.3Co2.7S4 (85 mV).[26] More impressively, V8C7@GC NSs/NF is way ahead to afford high current density Adv. Energy Mater. 2018, 1800575 Figure 3. TEM and HRTEM images of a,d) NH 4VO 3 NSs/NF, b,e) VO@GC NSs/NF, c,f) V 8C7@GC NSs/NF, respectively. The insets are the corresponding FFT and SAED patterns.
