www.advenergymat.de www.advancedsciencenews.com© 2018 WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim 1800575 (5 of 7) (100 mA cm−2), urgently needed for practical applications, with much lower η 100 (131 mV) than that of Pt (153 mV). A control experiment was conducted to confirm that the enhanced per - formance is due to the forming of single-crystalline V 8C7 rather than the introduction of carbon (Figure S12, Supporting Infor - mation). As shown in Figure 4d, the Tafel slopes of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF, Pt, and V 8C7 NSs/NF were 44.5, 49, and 58 mV dec−1, respectively. It is well-known that the Tafel slope is tightly asso- ciated with the reaction kinetics, and hence the similar Tafel slopes between Pt and V 8C7 further testify the platinum-like feature of V 8C7. Furthermore, the long-term stability is another imperative factor to appraise the HER electrocatalysts. Specifi- cally, as proved by chronoamperometry tests, the V 8C7@GC NSs/NF electrode could maintain its efficient HER activity for more than 100 h (Figure S13a, Supporting Information), which is due to the tiny changes in morphology (Figure S14, Supporting Information), and unchanged crystalline phase (Figure S15, Supporting Information). The inexistence of O in the energy dispersive X-ray (EDX) spectrum further veri-fies that the V 8C7 is not oxidized during the catalytic process (Figure S16, Supporting Information). The XPS analysis of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF after long-term durability test was con- ducted and showed in Figure S17 (Supporting Information), from which we could determine that V 8C7 did not suffer any oxidation during durability test and V 8C7 is the active ingredient providing actual active sites for HER. It is worth mentioning that such remarkable HER activity, e.g., low overpotential, low Tafel slope, and excellent long-term stability, is much better than those of other reported carbide, phosphide, sulfide, and selenide electrocatalysts (Table S4, Supporting Information). The electrochemical double layer capacitance (C dl) unmasks an electrochemical active surface area (ECSA) of V 8C7. Obviously, due to the single-crystal V 8C7 networks caused by decisive double-deck carbon coating, the C dl of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF (166 mF cm−2) is much higher than that of V 8C7 NSs/NF (85 mF cm−2) (Figure S18, Supporting Information). Besides, the electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) proves that the electronic resistance is sharply cut down via carbon coating (Figure S19, Supporting Information). Notably, V 8C7@GC NSs/NF also presents remarkable HER activity in neutral and acidic solutions, which is of vital impor - tance in some specific applications, e.g., water–alkali HER elec-trolyzers, seawater HER electrolyzers, and microbial electrolysis cells. As displayed in Figure 4b,c, the η 10 of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF at acidic and neutral media is 38 and 77 mV, respectively, which is better than other reported non-noble-metal-based HER elec- trocatalysts (Table S4, Supporting Information). Meanwhile, the Tafel slopes of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF in acidic and neutral media are 34.5 and 64 mV dec−1, respectively, which is comparable to, or surpass that of Pt. Surprisingly, the V 8C7@GC NSs/NF elec- trode also presents excellent durability in both acidic and neu-tral media (Figures S14–S17, Supporting Information). All the aforementioned results indicate that the dense V 8C7@GC NSs formed an effective protective layer for the intimal NF against acid etching, which contributes to the excellent HER durability in the acidic media. To the best of our knowledge, the V 8C7@ GC NSs/NF possess the excellent pH-universal HER perfor - mance among most of the non-noble metal-based HER catalyst (Table S4, Supporting Information). For understanding the HER processes in all media, DFT and nudged elastic band (NEB) methods are adopted. Gener - ally, it is widely accepted that the neutral HER shares the same mechanism with the alkaline one, thus we explore the HER mechanisms in the acidic and alkaline media. [27] Based on Adv. Energy Mater. 2018, 1800575 Figure 4. LSV curves of the V 8C7@GC NSs/NF, V 8C7 NSs/NF, Pt sheet, and NF in a) 1 m KOH, b) 0.1 m PBS, c) 0.5 m H2SO4. Tafel plots of the V 8C7@ GC NSs/NF, V 8C7 NSs/NF, and Pt sheet in d) 1 m KOH, e) 0.1 m PBS, f) 0.5 m H2SO4.
