www.advenergymat.de www.advancedsciencenews.com© 2018 WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim 1800575 (6 of 7) Adv. Energy Mater. 2018, 1800575the DFT calculation and Tafel slopes, V 8C7@GC NSs/NF in acidic medium follows the efficient Volmer (hydrogen adsorp- tion: H 3O+ + e− → H ads + H 2O) and the Tafel (chemical des- orption: H ads + H ads → H 2) reactions (Figure 5a,c).[28] Though the HER process has been widely learned in acid medium, the mechanism in alkaline solution has not been well investi- gated. Herein, based on the theoretical simulation and experi- mental results, we take V 8C7 as an example and put forward our understanding about the HER mechanism in alkaline electrolytes (Figure 5b) (see the Supporting Information Video for detail). [29] First, the H OH bond would be weakened due to the electronic effect of the interaction between the dangling C atom (Cδ−) and H atom, as well as interaction between the under-coordinated metal center (Vδ+) and O atom. Then, H 2O molecule dissociates into H atom and OH− with the help of a free electron. Following that, the OH− adsorbs on the Vδ+, while the H atom transfers onto a nearby Cδ− atom and becomes an adsorbed H (H ads). Finally, H 2 molecule is generated via the following Heyrovsky reaction or Tafel reaction. To further investigate the water dissociation in alkaline solutions, we have calculated the reaction path of water dissociation based on the NEB method. As illustrated in Figure 5d, the barrier energy for a single water molecule dissociation is as low as 0.16 eV, lower than that of Pt (0.51 eV), which reveals water molecule can be easily broken down, thus accelerating the slow rate of the Volmer step. [30] In conclusion, we demonstrated the novel, platinum-like, double-deck carbon enveloped V 8C7 networks, exposed with highly active (110) facet, for the first time. To the best of our knowledge, the single crystal V 8C7@GC NSs/NF exhibited best pH-universal HER performances among all non-noble metal-based HER catalysts. The excellent catalytic activity of V 8C7@GC NSs/NF is primarily due to the following reasons. I) The typical metallic behavior and single crystal feature of V 8C7 networks guarantee the rapidly electron transport. II) As verified by the high value of C dl, porous double-deck carbon layers and the beneficial C vacancy in V 8C7 crystal provide numerous catalytically active sites for catalytic reactions. III) V 8C7@GC NSs, exposed with (110) facet, could expose abun- dant catalytically accessible surface atomic sites, resulting in fast charge transport for HER. IV) Interweaved V 8C7 networks with designed morphology are tightly enveloped in double-deck graphitized carbon layers to form a sandwich-like construction, availably avoiding the oxidation of metallic V 8C7. Particularly, the V 8C7@GC NSs/NF deliver outstanding HER performances in an all-pH environment, comparable to or even better than that of Pt. In addition, the HER mechanism of platinum-like TMCs is well elaborated via theoretical simulation. All in all, this work opens up a new way to fabricate novel platinum-like TMCs for catalysis and energy conversion. Supporting Information Supporting Information is available from the Wiley Online Library or from the author. Acknowledgements This work was financially supported by the Fundamental Research Funds for the Central Universities (Grant No. 0301005202017), Thousand Young Talents Program of the Chinese Central Government (Grant No. 0220002102003), National Natural Science Foundation of China (NSFC, Grant Nos. 21373280 and 21403019), the Fundamental Research Figure 5. a) Schematic representation of the HER reaction mechanism in acidic media. b) Schematic illustration of water dissociation in alkaline solutions. c) Calculated free energy diagram for HER of different surfaces. The value of Pt is taken from ref. [20]. d) The reaction coordinate and the barrier energy of water dissociation.
