valence state of potassium, titanium, oxygen in K 2Ti8O17 material. The photocatalytic activity of KTO photocatalyst modiﬁed by metal (Pt, Au, Cu, Ag, Co) cocatalyst was evaluated for watersplitting under UV irradiation, which is shown in Fig. 4 a andthe hydrogen-evolution rate is 390.17, 375.05, 136.63, and 24.78 mmol mol catalyst/C01h/C01, respectively. The results indicate that metallic cocatalyst is of critical importance in deter-mining the activity of hydrogen evolution for water splittingunder UV irradiation. As a consequence, it is remarkably Fig. 2 e(a) TEM and (b) HRTEM images of KTO sample. Fig. 3 eXPS spectra of KTO sample.international journal of hydrogen energy xxx (2018) 1 e10 4 Please cite this article in press as: Yu Z, et al., A novel K 2Ti8O17nanorod photocatalyst rich in surface OH groups for efﬁcient hydrogen production by water splitting, International Journal of Hydrogen Energy (2018), https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2018.07.169
