temperature have a signiﬁcant effect on the formation of target K 2Ti8O17material. Additionally, the metallic cocatalyst is of critical importance in determining the activity ofhydrogen evolution. The 3 wt.% Pt/KTO photocatalyst exhibitthe highest hydrogen evolution rate as high as 390.17 mmolmol catalyst/C01h/C01. More importantly, it is found that the hydrogen evolution rate positively correlated the content of surface OHgroups of KTO samples with different thermal annealingtemperature. This could due to more amounts of surface OHgroups over KTO photocatalyst would generate more hydroxylradical, which react with CH 3OH to form CO, CH 4,C O 2un- dergoes $CH2OH radical intermediate. Thus, it is favor of preventing photo-generating electron and photo-generating hole from recombining. Moreover, KTO sample has goodsurface OH regeneration ability when it is contact with waterunder UV irradiation. Consequently, K 2Ti8O17exhibit better photocatalytic performance for water splitting under UV ra-diation. The work offers a novel insight to design theoutstanding photocatalytic performance photocatalyst forwater splitting. Acknowledgements We are grateful for the support of this work from the NationalNatural Science Foundation of China (No. 21773284, 21703276,51401233), the Shanxi Science and Technology Department(No. 2015081044), and the Hundred Talents Program of theChinese Academy of Sciences and Shanxi Province. Appendix A. Supplementary data Supplementary data related to this article can be found athttps://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2018.07.169 . references [1]Lee C, Um M, Kumazawa H. Synthesis of titanate derivatives using ion-exchange reaction. J Am Ceram Soc 2000;83:1098 e102. [2]Cao J, Wang A, Yin H, Shen L, Ren M, Han S, et al. Selective synthesis of potassium titanate whiskers starting frommetatitanic acid and potassium carbonate. Ind Eng Chem Res 2010;49:9128 e34. [3]Wang X, Liu S, Qi Y, Zhao L, Cui C. Behavior of potassium titanate whisker in simulated body ﬂuid. 