13792 |  Chem. Commun., 2021, 57, 13792–13795 This journal is © The Royal Society of Chemistry 2021 Cite this: Chem. Commun., 2021, 57, 13792A polyaniline-modified electrode surface for boosting the electrocatalysis towards thehydrogen evolution reaction and ethanol oxidation reaction † Yankun Huang, ‡aFeng Bao, ‡aMuwei Ji, *aYanzhao Hu,aLiu Huang,b Huichao Liu,aJiali Yu,aGuangtao Cong,aCaizhen Zhu *aand Jian Xu a Here, polyaniline (PANI) is reported loaded on carbon paper to modify the carbon paper-PANI-Pt electrode surface, tailoring theelectrocatalytic capability towards the hydrogen evolution reactionand ethanol oxidation reaction. The reasons for the enhancementby the PANI layer are attributed to the hydrophilic electrode sur-face, uniform dispersion of Pt, and large electrochemical activesurface. The structure and properties of electrode surfaces are impor- tant for electrocatalysis due to the molecular absorption andmass transport. 1,2Besides the works on catalyst exploration for water splitting, rechargeable batteries and electrochemicalorganic synthesis, electrode surface modification is one of theimportant factors to enhance the performance in thesefields. 3–5In order to obtain catalysis with excellent activity and durability, lots of work has been carried out towardsexploring new catalysts, such as non-novel metals. 6–8Never- theless, the surface modification of electrodes to investigate theelectrochemistry and enhancing the nanocrystals is also aninteresting topic in this field. 9,10During the electrocatalysis of the methanol oxidation reaction on a Pt surface, the active siteson the Pt surface will be coordinated with CO or other mole-cules and then the reaction kinetics of electrocatalysis are reduced. 11How to reduce the CO absorption on Pt is still a great challenge. Meanwhile, it is expected to promote the absorption of the reactive molecules. Such selective absorptiondepends on the structures and properties of the electrodesurface. Furthermore, the interaction of catalysts and supportsis also a possible factor to enhance the electrocatalysis becausea good electrode surface can promote the electron and masstransport during electrocatalysis. As reported by Monge-Romero et al., 12polyaniline (PANI) and polypyrole were employed to boost the electrochemical performance viamod- ifying the electrode surface. Furthermore, Li et al. reported a three-layered PtPd/PPy/PtPd hybrid catalyst that presentedincreased electrocatalytic activity toward small organic mole-cules due to its unique structure for rapidly transporting the active species along short diffusion paths, as well as its large exposed surface area. 13Rajendra et al. developed Pd 30Pt29Au41/ PPY and found that the high activity was attributed to theformation of Pt–Pd–Au heterojunctions and the strong inter-actions between the PPY nanofibers. 1,2El-Anadouli reported Pt/PANI nanocatalysts for electrocatalysis of the formic acidoxidation reaction. 14,15Introducing PANI into the catalyst can significantly enhance the catalytic activity of the catalyst towards the formic acid oxidation reaction by shifting the mechanism towards the desirable pathway and mitigating theundesirable poisoning pathway. 15The electrocatalytic oxida- tion proved that the combination of Pt and conductive poly-mers could enhance the catalytic activity, where the increasingactivity was related to the improvement of the Pt particledistribution and the electronic chemical active surfacearea. 16,17Therefore, the metallic catalyst provided catalytic sites and the conductive polymers tailored the properties on absorb-ing molecules. The synergetic interaction of the catalysts andconductive polymer support enhances the electrochemical per-formance of polymer-modified electrodes. In addition, organicmaterials were also used to modify the electrode for electro-chemical organic synthesis such as Diels-Alder reaction andSuzuki reaction, 1,2which proved the significant role of organic compounds or polymers modifying electrodes. Hence, the sur- face modification of electrodes with a conductive polymer would bring some specific and controllable properties. Toinvestigate the polymer-modified electrode surface and theeffect on the electrochemistry, we loaded PANI on carbon paper(CP) and then studied the effect on the electrochemical growthof Pt nanocrystals. As shown in Fig. 1A, aniline wasaInstitute of Low-Dimensional Materials Genome Initiative, College of Chemistry and Environmental Engineering, Shenzhen University, Shenzhen, 518060, China.E-mail: jimuwei@163.com, czzhu@szu.edu.cn bSchool of Chemistry and Chemical Engineering, Guangdong Pharmaceutical University, Zhongshan, 528458, China †Electronic supplementary information (ESI) available. See DOI: 10.1039/d1cc04163k ‡These authors contributed equally to this work.Received 11th August 2021, Accepted 26th November 2021 DOI: 10.1039/d1cc04163k rsc.li/chemcommChemComm COMMUNICATION Published on 29 November 2021. Downloaded by Beijing University of Chemical Technology on 3/29/2026 2:23:58 AM. View Article Online View Journal | View Issue
