mediated method. Lu et al. [ 35] prepared the Au–Pd core– shell heterostructures with HIFs using Au nanocubes as thestructure-directing cores. And the ascorbic acid and cetyltrimethylammonium chloride (CTAC) were used as the reducing agent and surfactant, respectively. The Pdshell was bounded by high-index {730} facets and formed via Ostwald ripening in the presence of dissolved oxygen and chloride ions, as shown in Fig. 5. The oxidative etch- ing process can protect the HIFs, which can be ascribed to that the surfactant adsorbed the facets of Pd. The polyhe- dron-aggregated multi-facet Cu 2O structures enclosed by high-index {522} facets were reported by Sun’s group [ 36]. The OH-concentration of sodium hydroxide has signiﬁ- cant effect on the controlling the growth of different facets through seed-mediated strategy, which produced the multi- facets structures. 3.1.2 Selectively etching metal atoms The selectively etching mainly focused the nucleation and growth process, thereby adjusting the structures and sizes of NCs. In the process, the addition of oxidation etchants(Cl -/O2) selectively adsorbed at special sites and facets and hence regulating growth mechanism, which changes the morphologies of NCs. Xiong’s group [ 37] has demonstrated that oxidative etching possesses an effect on achievement of both uniform shape and size. They foundthat the role of oxidative etching by Cl-/O2can selectively remove twinned particles, due to higher energy than that ofsingle crystal. Moreover, they reported that the presence of chloride could obtain the high yield single crystal silver NCs, which was ascribed to the enhanced oxidizing prop-erty of solution [ 38]. Xiong [ 39] reported that the oxygen dissolved in the solution can slightly oxidizes and etch atoms on the corners of Ag nanocubes and then generatetruncated cubes. According to the previous literature, when deionized water was introduced into the reaction system, the amount of Cl -/O2pairs could increase, which could improve the corrosion rate of surface atoms and facilitate the formation of high-index facets [ 40]. The Br-/O2,C l-/ O2,F e2?/Fe3?and Cu?/Cu2?were used as an oxidizing etchant in several studies [ 41–43]. Considering the above literatures, the high-index facets can be formed throughoxidative etching process, excess Cl -/O2pairs selectively adsorbed on to the {100} facets as well as may diffuse onto the neighbored {111} facets, and then high-index facets areretained [ 44]. The halide ions, as capping agent, selectively adsorb on the facets of nanocrystalline, for example, the Br -and Cl- can selectively adsorb onto {100} facet of Pt and Pd nanocrystals. It hinders the reduction and deposition of atoms on the speciﬁc facets of nucleation, thus changingthe surface free energy and regulating the growth rate of speciﬁc facets, thereby inﬂuencing the morphologies ofTable 2 Projection angles and geometrical parameters of different structure with HIFs Polyhedral projection directionGeometrical model of polyhedronEquation for projection angles and Miller indicesCalculated projectionangles TOH\110[ a¼2arctanﬃﬃ 2p h h/C01/C16/C17 b=9 0/C176-(a=2)?(c/2) c¼2arctanﬃﬃ 2p h 1/C16/C17{hhl} ab c {221} 141 /C176 90/C176 141/C176 {552} 134 /C176 97/C176 148.5 /C176 {331} 129.5 /C176 102/C176 153.5 /C176 {441} 124 /C176 108/C176 160/C176 HOH\110[ a¼2arctanﬃﬃ 2p h k/C01/C16/C17 b=9 0/C176-(a=2)? c¼2arctan1ﬃﬃ 2p lkþhðÞhi{hkl} ab c {321} 153.5 /C176 87.45 /C176 148.4 /C176 {421} 160.0 /C176 86.75 /C176 153.5 /C176 {431} 141.1 /C176 98.0/C176 157.1 /C176 {432} 160.0 /C176 78.0/C176 136.0 /C176 {532} 163.9 /C176 78.6/C176 141.1 /C176 THH\100[ a¼2arctanh k/C0/C1 b= 270 /C176-a{hk0} ab {210} 126.9 /C176 143.1 /C176 {520} 136.4 /C176 133.6 /C176 {320} 143.1 /C176 126.9 /C176 {720} 148.1 /C176 121.9 /C176 {410} 151.9 /C176 118.1 /C176 1 Rare Met.A review of energy and environment electrocatalysis based on high-index faceted nanocrystals
