reported representative works about NCs enclosed with HIFs and their outstanding applications in ORR ﬁeld. As shown in Fig. 14, it can be seen that the concave decahedron (CCD) Pt 3Ni NCs possesses the highest ORR performance [ 108]. The reason is that, on the one hand, the (111) plane of Pt 3Ni is an ideal catalytic place for ORR, on the other hand, the concave structure possesses amounts ofstepped surface atoms, which provides more adsorbed/ desorbed active sites for reactant. However, the average- level ORR performance of concave cube reveals that, forORR, the HIFs is an important factor to improve the cat- alytic performance, not the decisive factor. Under the guidance of above conclusions, many synergistic strategiesof design principle for ORR performance were reported recently. Among all synthesis strategies, the wet-chemistry method, especially hydrothermal synthesis, is the most widely applied. Thus, many representative works spring up like mushrooms. As shown in Fig. 15a–d, Xie’s group reported that a simple cetyltrimethylammonium bromide- assisted method is proposed to controllably synthesize PtCo alloy NCs with a unique excavated octahedral shape[109]. The excavated octahedral PtCo alloy NCs were intrinsically built with mutually perpendicular interlaced ultrathin PtCo nanosheets bound with {100} facets that arenot the thermodynamically most stable for face-centered cubic metals. In addition, the crystal indices will change with the increase in Pt:Ni ratio, as shown in Fig. 15e, of which PtCo possesses a complete excavated octahedral structure. The electrochemically surface area of the unique excavated octahedral PtCo alloy NCs is determined to be23.3 m 2/C1g-1 Pt, which is signiﬁcantly larger than that of the Fig. 13 TEM images of aPt3Mn CNCs, e0.4%Mo/Pt 3Mn,b, cPt3Mn and f0.4%Mo/Pt 3Mn after 28,000 s stability test; EDS elemental mapping images of dPt3Mn and g0.4%Mo/Pt 3Mn catalyst after 28,000 s stability test; hsurface illustration of Pt 3Mn CNC and M