talyst for water splitting, synthesized via ahydrothermal-selenization two-step route. The composite presents a dense array of bulky CoS 2and MoS 2nanoarrays Figure 3: Schematic illustration of the synthesis processes and characterization of FeCo –Ni5P4@C–CNFs. A (a) Graphical sketch of the preparation process of (Ni,Fe)S 2/NiFe-CNFs (b) SEM image (c) TEM image (d) HRTEM image, and (e) EDX mappings60Copyright © 2025, Elsevier. B (a) Scheme of the synthetic process of FeCo –Ni5P4@C–CNFs (b –c) HRTEM images (d) FESEM image (e) EDS mapping images of FeCo –Ni5P461Copyright © 2025, American Chemical Society. C (a) Schematic synthetic illustration of the 3Ni@NiO/CNFs material (b) FESEM image and (c) lattice fringes62Copyright © 2025, American Chemical Society.8 M. Murad et al.: Transition metal compounds-carbon
