Renewable and Sustainable Energy Reviews 161 (2022) 112323 20and 241 mV at 10 mA/cm2, and Tafel slopes of 46 and 59 mV/dec, respectively. Moreover, when Ni3FeN-NPs electrodes were used bifunctionally, a cell voltage of 1.81 V was needed to achieve 10 mA/cm2. Also, the as-fabricated water electrolyzer exhibited stable electrocatalytic performance without deterioration in 1 M KOH after 130 h. The basic functionality behind the bifunctional electrocatalysis has been illustrated in Fig. 31. In another study [190], a SS mesh consisting of vertically woven SS fibres with a diameter of 26 μm and a smooth surface was used as a substrate for electrocatalyst. The surface of the 3D SS mesh was modified by depositing carbon nanotubes (CNTs) for efficient water splitting. To increase the HER activity, Zhang et al. [190] deposited platinum on the surface of oxidized CNT/SS . The polarization curve indicated that the Pt/OxCNT/SS required an overpotential of 56 mV to reach a current density of 10 mA cm␀2. Other samples, i.e. OxCNT/SS, CNT/SS, bare SS, and 20 wt% Pt/C/SS, had higher overpotentials of 257, 334, 359, and 82 mV, respectively. The as-prepared Pt/OxCNT/SS exhibited the best HER performance when compared to other SS-based electrodes as re- ported in the literature. ECSA was suspected to be the prime cause of the enhanced activity of the surface [191]. A 1.5–50 times higher Cdl value for the Pt/OxCNT/SS suggested that the modification of the SS and coupling with Pt could increase the ECSA. Similarly, the Cdl of the OxCNT/SS was higher than that of the CNT/SS, which suggested that the presence of oxygen on the surface of the CNT could have enhanced the ECSA for HER. For water splitting in a neutral electrolyte, the Pt/OxCNT/SS and RuO 2/OxCNT/SS showed overpotentials of 52 and 410 mV to reach a current density of 10 mA/cm2 for the HER and OER, respectively. It was concluded that the Pt/OxCNT/SS || RuO 2/OxCNT/SS cell configuration needed 1.50 and 1.70 V to obtain a current 