37. The Co2P catalyst did not present a notable variation in the HER over- potential in both media after extended cycling. Furthermore, it was evident that to achieve the benchmark current density of 10 mA cm␀2, the overpotentials of 120 mV and 70 mV were required in acidic and alkaline media, respectively. Very few researchers have established the interdependence of pH and stability of stainless steel in corrosive environments and water splitting reactions [206]. However, the electrochemical behavior of austenitic Cr23N1.2 steel exposed to 3.5% NaCl solutions was studied. It was concluded that in highly acidic solutions with pH 1–2 for Cr23N1.2 and at рН 1 for Cr18Ni9, the steels were highly active and this fact was indicated by a high current density and an active-passive transition in Fig. 32.(a) Blank, untreated 316 steel; (b–d) steel 316 immersed into NaOH and (NH 4)2S2O8 mixture for 6 h (b), 12 h (c) and 18 h (d) respectively, Scale bar, 500 nm [157]. Fig. 33.Polarization curve in a two-electrode system with SS mesh anode & Ni foam cathode [192]. A. Raza et al.
