ChemistrySelectResearch Article doi.org/10.1002/slct.202405005 deposited more uniformly on the fiber filament surface.[26]On the other hand, in order to fully evaluate the long-term stability oftheelectrode,wetestedthetypicalsamplePt-SSF-0.1fordura- bility under more extreme conditions and tested the XPS, SEM, and ICP after the long-term durability test. As shown in Figure S2 and Table S1, after a 72 h chronopotentiometric durability test in 1MK O Ha tac o n s t a n tc u r r e n td e n s i t yo f1 0 0m A · c m−2, Pt-SSF-0.1 shows good long-term durability, and all these results prove that Pt-SSF-0.1 has good electrochemical stability. 4.Conclusions In conclusion, we have successfully used a simple, efficient, and convenient electrodeposition method to prepare self-supported electrodesbydepositingPtonstainlesssteelfiberfeltsubstrates, allowing them to produce hydrogen in 1 M KOH. The three- dimensional structure of the SSF facilitates mass and charge transfer in the electrolytic water reaction. The overpotential of Pt-SSF-0.1 for HER at 10 mA·cm−2in 1 M KOH is just 21 mV. In addition, the Pt-SSF-0.1 electrode also showed excellent elec- trochemical stability in the 12 h stability test. The prominent activity of the prepared self-supported electrodes makes them promising for industrial water electrolysis. Acknowledgements The authors are grateful for the financial support provided by Central Guiding Local Science and Technology Development Foundation of China (ZYYD2025QY13). ConflictofInterests The authors declare no conflict of interest. DataAvailabilityStatement The data that support the findings of this study are available from the corresponding author upon reasonable request. Keywords: Electrodeposition •Hydrogen evolution reaction • Self-supported electrode •Stainless steel fiber felt [1] Z. Xing, Q. Li, D. Wang, X. Yang, X. Sun, Electrochim. Acta 2016,191,8 4 1 – 845. [ 2 ] J .J .C a i ,Q .Y .Z h o u ,B .L i u ,X .F .G o n g ,Y .L .Z h a n g ,K .G o h ,D .M .G u