aterials to commercialization is the relatively complex electrode preparation  method ( i.e. particles loading onto a glassy carbon elect rode) and limited industrial -scale production  capacity . In contrast, our flexible and self -supported HEMGs are produced by an industrial -scale metallurgical technique  (from tons to million of tons)  and employ  a simple dealloying process to achieve HER activities that are  much better than alternative noble metal -based electrocatalysts  (Figure 4d) , demonstrating their great potential for near term commercialization.  Furthermore , the dealloyed nanosponge -like HEMG provide d excellent stability performance  with the overpotential amplifications of only ~10 mV
