sult. Additional experiments were performed to provide further understanding of the mechanism. A crucial parameter for evaluating HER performance is the exchange current density ( j0), which is determined by fitting LSV data to the Tafel equation [15]. The exchange current densities of all samples are listed in Table S4 (in the ESM). The j0 values of all Rh-Au-SiNW catalysts are larger than those of the Au-SiNW catalyst. The Rh-Au-SiNW-2 catalyst showed the second largest apparent exchange current density, j0,app, of 47.9 μA·cm–2 (less than only j0,app = 409 μA·cm–2 for 40 wt.% Pt/C), which is 5.38 and 2.40 times greater than that of the Au-SiNW and Figure 3  (a) LSV curves for the HER with various catalysts in N 2-saturated 0.5 M H 2SO 4, (b) the corresponding Tafel plots derive d from (a), and (c) the mass activity of five catalysts at an overpotential of 0.3 V .
