Thermo Scientific K-Alpha X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy (XPS) in- strument. The analysis was conducted under a chamber pressure of 5 × 10␀9 mbar. A monochromated Al-Kα X-ray source (15 kV, 150 W) with a spot size of 0.5 mm diameter was used to irradiate the samples during acquisition.2.7. Electrochemical measurements A potentiostat Metrohm Autolab PGSTAT 204 electrochemical setup with NOVA 2.0 as an operating software was used to evaluate the electrochemical analysis of HER. Three electrode systems were employed for electrochemical analysis: a GCE (3 mm in diameter) as a Fig. 2.SEM images with corresponding elemental composition tables for (a) Ti3AlC 2 MAX powder, (b) Ti3C2Tx, (c) GO, (d) rGO, (e) Ti3C2Tx/rGO, and (f) Pt/ Ti3C2Tx/rGO.F.E. Ab Latif et al.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              International  Journal  of Hydrogen  Energy  174 (2025)  151393 4
