illustrated in Fig. 3 (e), reveals thin layers of sheets with a well distributed small white dots, showing a well deposited Pt NPs on a network-like structure, which is vital in offering excellent ion trans - portation with abundant active sites for the catalytic activity during HER reactions [18,33,42]. The EDX mapping of 10Pt/Ti 3C2Tx/rGO electro - catalyst, depicted in Fig. 3 (f-l), shows the distribution of C, Ti, O, F, and Pt, further confirming the deposition of Pt NPs on the surface of the composite, which appear as white particles in Fig. 2 (f). 3.3. XRD and XPS analysis Fig. 4 (a)presents the diffractogram of the Ti3AlC2 MAX, where it has typical characteristics of phase diffraction at the plane (002), (004), (101), (104), (105), (109), and (110) with the two theta values of 9.7•, 19.2•, 34.1•, 39.0•, 41.9•, 56.5•, and 60.4•, respectively. These peaks are well-matched to the JCPDS No. 52-0875 standard, supporting the pure MAX powder used in this work. Notably, the synthesis of Ti3C2Tx through microwave-assisted hydrothermal heating is confirmed when the intensity peak at 41.9•for the (104) plane is reduced, indicating the elimination of the Al content. The observation for the Al peak reduction agrees well with the existing studies on the MXene synthesis through another approach [43]. Additionally, removing the Al layer during the etching process in- volves shifting the (002) plane towards the lower diffraction angles, suggesting an increment of the c lattice parameters due to the enlarge - ment of the interlayer spacing. From Fig. 4 (a), the peak at 9.7•for the (002) plane of Ti3AlC2 MAX has an interlayer d-spacing of 0.91 nm (calculated using Bragg ’s Law shown in Eqn (1)) and has shifted to 6.55• with an interlayer d-spacing of 1.35 nm. The enlargement of the inter- layer spacing is attributed to the introduction of the terminal functional groups (-O, -F, and -OH) at the Ti3C2Tx galleries. Furthermore, as evi- denced in the EDX analysis of the Ti3C2Tx, only 0.84 % of the initial Al remains in the final Ti3C2Tx, which can be considered negligible. The FESEM image of the Ti3C2Tx (shown in Fig. 2 (b)) also clearly depicts the typical morphology for the 2D Ti3C2Tx sheets, with crumpled, wrinkled, and thin-layered sheets, which are also aligned with previous findings [23]. Considering these findings, it can be said that the synthesis of the 2D Ti3C2Tx succeeded. Fig. 4.XRD patterns of (a) Ti3AlC 2 MAX and Ti3C2Tx, (b) GO and rGO, and (c) a combination of rGO, Ti3C2Tx, Ti3C2Tx/rGO, and Pt/Ti 3C2Tx/rGO. XPS spectra: (d) survey spectrum, (e) Ti 2p, (f) C 1s, (g) O 1s, (h) F 1s, and (i) Pt 4f.F.E. Ab Latif et al.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              International  Journal  of Hydrogen  Energy  174 (2025)  151393 7
