erences (PDF) ■AUTHORINFORMATION Corresponding Authors RezaAbazari −Department ofChemistry, FacultyofScience, University ofMaragheh, Maragheh 83111-55181, Iran; orcid.org/0000-0002-3725-2557; Email:abazari@ maragheh.ac.ir JinjieQian −KeyLaboratory ofCarbonMaterials ofZhejiang Province, CollegeofChemistry andMaterials Engineering, Wenzhou University, Wenzhou, Zhejiang325035,PR China; orcid.org/0000-0002-9996-7929; Email:jinjieqian@wzu.edu.cn Authors SoheilaSanati −Department ofChemistry, FacultyofScience, University ofMaragheh, Maragheh 83111-55181, IranNanLi−KeyLaboratory ofCarbonMaterials ofZhejiang Province, CollegeofChemistry andMaterials Engineering, Wenzhou University, Wenzhou, Zhejiang325035,PRChina Complete contactinformation isavailableat: https://pubs.acs.org/10.1021/acs.inorgchem.3c03052 Notes Theauthorsdeclarenocompeting financialinterest. ■ACKNOWLEDGMENTS Thisworkwassupported byUniversity ofMaragheh, Iran’s National ElitesFoundation andIranNational Science Foundation (projectnumber: 4025093 and4025105). The authorsarealsogratefulforthefinancialsupport. ■REFERENCES (1)Liu,N.;Chai,L.;Senthil,R.A.;Li,W.;Krishnamoorthy, M.; Sun,Y.;Liu,X.;Qian,J.;Li,X.;Pan,J.Coupleofnonpolarized/ polarized electrodes buildinganewuniversal electrochemical energy storagesystemwithanimpressive energydensity.ACSAppl.Mater. Interfaces 2021,13,45375−45384. (2)Chen,K.;Downes, C.A.;Goodpaster, J.D.;Marinescu, S.C. Hydrogen Evolving ActivityofDithiolene-Based Metal−Organic Frameworks withMixedCobaltandIronCenters.Inorg.chem.2021, 60,11923−11931. (3)Megía,P.J.;Vizcaíno, A.J.;Calles,J.A.;Carrero,A.Hydrogen Production Technologies: FromFossilFuelsTowardRenewable Sources.Aminireview.EnergyFuels2021,35,16403−16415. (4)Chen,D.;Han,C.;Sun,Q.;Ding,J.;Huang,Q.;Li,T.T.;Hu, Y.;Qian,J.;Huang,S.Bimetallic AgNinanoparticles anchored onto MOF-derived nitrogen-doped carbonnanostrips forefficienthydro- genevolution. GreenEnergyEnvironment 2023,8,258−266. (5)Fujishima, A.;Honda,K.Electrochemical Photol