NPNs’ morphology was observed using a JEM-2100F transmission electron microscope (TEM) whose samples were prepared by depositing ultra-dilute NPNs (mix ed with ethanol) onto carbon copper grids. NPNs’ molar ratio of Ni to P(n(Ni):n(P)) was determined using a Thermo iCAP6300inductively coupled plasma optical emission spectrometer (ICP). C. Working electrodes and electrochemical measurements NPNs of different annealing times and Pt/C (purchased from Hispec 3000, 20 wt. %), diluted by ethanol, served as electrode materials that were uniformly dropped on T-shaped glasscarbon electrodes (GCE, 5 mm in diameter). Then, the working electrodes whose catalysts’mass density was 0.6 mg/cm 2were sealed by 10 ll of Naﬁon solution (2 wt. %, 100 ll). A series of electrochemical measurements were carried out using a CHI 660D electrochemical worksta-tion. The electrolyte was comprised of either 0.5 M sulfuric acid (H 2SO4) or 1 M NaOH which was pre-aerated by N 2to create an almost nigh-oxygen-free condition. The measuring system consisted of a classical three-electrode glass cell. The reference electrode was either a saturatedAg/AgCl electrode (SSCE) in the acidic condition or a saturated calomel electrode (SCE) in the alkaline condition. The HER activity of different working electrodes in different testing stages was determined by linear sweep voltammetry (LSV) by which polarization curves could beplotted. The scanning voltage was /C01.05 to /C01.6 V in NaOH and /C00.15 to /C00.65 V in H 2SO4. The durability of normal hydrogen nickel scales (NHNs) was tested by 500 cycles potentiostaticexperiment outputs the time-dependent current density curve. In order to obtain more insightinto the electrochemical properties, electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) was applied,with applied frequencies of 0.1 to 10 5Hz. All the potentials given in this work were converted to the reversible hydrogen electrode (RHE), and all the electrochemical data measured in experiments were tested without any iRcompensation. In 0.5 M H 2SO4, E (RHE) ¼E (SSCE) þ(0.197 þ0.059 pH), and in NaOH, E (RHE) ¼E (SCE) þ(0.242 þ0.059 pH). III. RESULTS AND DISCUSSION In TGA measurements, the exchange of materials between the sample under investigation and the environmental matter may be possible and one should take care of good precautions;for example, one should put a covered-crucible with an open-lid to prevent any exchange. Ifthe exchange occurs, it will appear as the parasitic peak(s) super loaded on the original smoothcurve. Fortunately, the curve illustrated in Fig. 1shows the TGA-data as a function of tempera- ture with smooth and consecutive slide behavior. This means that there is no parasitic exchangein our curve. We have chosen an annealing temperature at 350 /C14C where the curve has the max- imum smooth and consecutive slide behavior. Pirkkalainen et al. have reported that the fcc Ni phase crystallized below 573 K after which also maxima possibly arising from the hcp Ni phase FIG. 1. DSC/TGA curves of the as-prepared NPNs.023104-3 Abdalla, Al-Marzouki, and Obaid J. Renewable Sustainable Energy 9, 023104 (2017)
