annealed samples are shown in Figs. 3(g), 3(h), and 3(i) . Clearly, both nickel and phosphorus are uniformly distributed amid these nanoparticles. Fig. 4shows the polarization curves of vari- ous working electrodes measured in 0.5 M H 2SO4. The HER activity of a bare GCE can be almost neglected. As it has been expected, the Pt/C catalyst displays the greatest HER property, which requires only /C0135 mV to reach /C0100 mA/cm2(g100¼135 mV). For samples heat treated for different periods of time, HER activity actually increases with the extension of the annealing time. As to original non-annealed NPNs, g100 is 334 mV and its 4-h heat treated equivalent is 313 mV. The 8-h annealed sample displays a further upgradation in terms of HERactivity, with just 251 mV of g100, which is excellent and comparable with those of Ni-P nano- particles and other metal phosphide nanoparticles reported. Table S1 ( supplementary material ) compares HER activities of a series of metal phosphides, which takes into account the massdensity of the catalysts, substrate, and electrolyte. From the data in Table S1 ( supplementary material ) which shows NPNs’ superior HER activity and the NPNs’ low-cost preparation pro- cess, it is found that the materials produced in this work have struck a balance among differentnecessary conditions. Meanwhile, the conversion efﬁciency 32—is 78 mV. The 8-h annealing sample’s onset potential g2, usually deﬁned as the value of potential when the current reaches /C02 mA/cm2,33,34is 21 mV. The HER behavior of the samples tested in NaOH is much lower than that tested in H 2SO4, as can be observed in Fig. 5, but they still show comparatively nice properties. For the 8-h annealing sample, g50¼434 mV. FIG. 3. TEM pictures of NPNs: (a) non-heat-treated NPNs; (b) non-heat-treated NPNs with higher resolution; (d) 4-h-heat- treated NPNs; (e) 8-h-heat-treated NPNs. HRTEM pictures: (c) non-annealed sample; (f) 8-h annealed sample, in which the inset is the corresponding FFT image. STEM images: (g1), (g2), and (g3) non-annealed NPNS; (h1), (h2), and (h3) 4-h- annealed NPNs; and (i1), (i2), and (i3) 8-h-annealed NPNs. FIG. 4. Polarization curves of NPNs heat treated by different times, Pt/C and GCE in 0.5 M H 2SO4.023104-5 Abdalla, Al-Marzouki, and Obaid J. Renewable Sustainable Energy 9, 023104 (2017)
