Polymerization of EDOT to PEDOT Iron(III) tris epetoluenesulfonate (Fe(OTs) 3) was ﬁrst prepared by reﬂuxing pre-treated Fe(OH) 3from Ferric chloride and so- dium hydroxide with petoluene sulfonic acid in methanol medium [37]. The polymerization of EDOT to PEDOT has then conducted in accordance the following procedure. Themixture of EDOT eFe(OTs) 3(1e2 (mol/mol)) was severely stir- red, subsequently treated by a hotplate stirrer at 50/C14C for 3 h for polymerization and continuously stirred for further 24 h at room temperature. The ﬁnal polymer was thoroughly washed with methanol and subsequently with distilled water toremove the present impurities. At last, poly(3,4 eethylene dioxythiophene) (PEDOT) was dried under room temporalvacuum conditions for 3 h. Preparation of PtNPs/PEDOT xeSG(1-x) Homogenous dispersions of PEDOT and SG with various com- positions of 100, 70, 50, 30 and 0 wt% of PEDOT in 10 mL of N,Nedimethylformamide (DMF) were ultrasonically prepared and dried at 80/C14C under vacuum conditions. The resulting different compositions of PEDOT-SG were decorated by plat-inum nanoparticles (PtNPs) using chemical reducing method,as follow: 100.0 mg of PEDOT eSG composite and 80.0 mg of dissolvedK 2PtCl 6were ﬁrst dispersedin 100.0 mL distilledwater under severe stirring. 200.0 mL of ethylene glycol was thenadded to the former suspension and further dispersed underultrasonic waves for 1 h until the suspension became uniform.After that, it was vigorously stirred at 120 /C14C during 12 h so that the Pt(II) ions reduced to PtNPs. The produced nanocomposite, assigned as PtNPs/PEDOT x-SG (1-x) (x can be 0.0 e1.0), was ﬁltered, repeatedly washed with distilled water, and ﬁnallydried under room temporal vacuum conditions [38]. Preparation of PtNPs/PEDOT xeSG(1-x)/GCE 2.0 mg of each PtNPs/PEDOT xeSG(1-x) was thoroughly dispersed in 1.0 mL distilled water-ethanol mixture at anultrasound bath during 5.0 min to get the homogeneous sus- pension. 10 mL of each prepared suspension was put on a pretreated glassy carbon electrode (with a diameter of1.6 mm), which was polished by 0.3 mm alumina slurry andrinsed with distilled water. After drying the modiﬁed GCEs atroom temperature, they were used for HER applications. Results and discussion The preparation of PtNPs/PEDOT x-SG (1-x)nanocomposite and electrochemical HER application of it was instrumentally investigated using different spectral techniques of FT-IR,Raman, EDS, XPS and XRD, microscopic images of SEM andTEM and electrochemical analyses of CV, LSV, and EIS. Characterization of PtNPs/PEDOT xeSG(1-x)nanocomposite The step by step characterization of prepared PEDOT-SG composite was investigated by FT eIR spectra of pristine graphite (a), sulfonated graphene (SG) (b), PEDOT (c), andPEDOT eSG (d) were exhibited in Fig. 1 A. The characterizing IR bands of C eO, C]C, CeH, and O eH contained in graphene sheets are located in 1100, 1575, 2900, and 3300 e3500 cm /C01, respectively. As can be observed in this ﬁgure, sulfonation-related bonds of SG are placed at 1316, 1283, 1178 and1068 cm /C01[39]. In addition, the O-H bond of sulfonic acid (eSO3H) can be indicated at around 3425 cm/C01as an intense wide band. However, the presence of intercalated water canbe overlapped by this band, which distinction of these bands from each other is not possible. It was, nevertheless, mini- mized by drying the product under vacuum conditions for3.0 h. Also, the presence of sulfonic group was also conﬁrmedby S]O stretching vibration at 1178 and 1068 cm /C01. Moreover, the synthesis of PEDOT and its coupling with SG were moni-tored by the observable bands centered at 976, 834, and680 cm /C01(CeS bond in the thiophene ring), 1118 and 1084 cm/C01(CeOeC stretching bond of the ethylene dioxy group), as well as 1509 and 1318 cm/C01(C]C and C eC Fig. 1eA): FTeIR spectra of pristine graphite (a), sulfonated graphene (SG) (b), PEDOT (c), and PEDOT eSG (d) in the range of 400e4000 cm¡1, as KBr pellets; B): Raman spectra of pristine graphite and sulfonated graphene (SG).international journal of hydrogen energy xxx (2018) 1 e10 3 Please cite this article in press as: Abdolmaleki A, et al., Efﬁcient and stable HER electrocatalyst using Pt-nanoparticles@poly(3,4 e- ethylene dioxythiophene) modiﬁed sulfonated graphene nanocomposite, International Journal of Hydrogen Energy (2018), https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2018.03.142
