stretching vibrations of the thiophene ring). It is notable that absorptions belong to SG included in the PEDOT eSG is not facilely distinguishable owing to overlapping with strongbands of PEDOT. The Raman spectra also conﬁrmed the edge-selective functionalization; they provided useful information on thestructural defects of the sp 2domains (D-peak), the in-plane vibration of sp2carbon atoms (G-peak) and the stacking or- ders (2D-peak) ( Fig. 1 B). The pristine graphite included a very weak D peak located at around 1350 cm/C01with the I D/IGratios of 0.54, whereas SG represented a strong D peak placed ataround 1365 cm /C01. Moreover, the intensity ratio of the D to G peaks was 2.72. It suggested the edge distortion and intro- duction of sp3-hybridized carbon atoms into the sp2-hybrid- ized SG layers by functionalization [40]. The shape of the 2Dband is known as a key parameter to determine the layer numbers of the graphene sheets. The peak position of the 2D band at 2723 cm/C01and nearly symmetrical shape of the peak provided evidence for the successful exfoliation of three-dimensional graphite into two-dimensional graphene-likesheets with covalent functionalization. It proposed thatRaman G peak of doped graphene was sensitive to molecularcharge-transfer, and also a red shift (~10 cm /C01), which was found in the G band of SG [40e42]. Graphene nanosheets and sulfonated ones are exhibited in scanning and transmission electron micrographs in accor-dance with Fig. 2 . SEM images for graphene before and after sulfonation are shown in Fig. 2 A and B, respectively. A typical SEM image of the pristine graphite had a ﬂake-shape withsmooth surfaces. Following the sulfonation reaction, the Fig. 2eSEM images of graphene nanosheets (A) and sulfonated graphene nanosheets (B); TEM images of graphene nanosheets (C), and sulfonated graphene nanosheets (D); TEM image of PtNPs decorated PEDOT-SG (E); and particle sized distribution of PtNPs (F).international journal of hydrogen energy xxx (2018) 1 e10 4 Please cite this article in press as: Abdolmaleki A, et al., Efﬁcient and stable HER electrocatalyst using Pt-nanoparticles@poly(3,4 e- ethylene dioxythiophene) modiﬁed sulfonated graphene nanocomposite, International Journal of Hydrogen Energy (2018), https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijhydene.2018.03.142
