with other reports in literature as given in Table 1 . As can be seen, its performance was close to the platinum electrode. Conclusions Summarily, a series of nanocomposite contained in platinum nanoparticles decorated poly(3,4 eethylene dioxythiophene)- sulfonated graphene (PtNPs/PEDOT x-SG (1-x)) (x is between 0.0 and 1.0) was prepared. This nanocomposite was successfullycharacterized by FT-IR, Raman, EDS, XPS, SEM, TEM and CV. The activities of these nanocomposites as HER electro- catalysts were evaluated using LSV and EIS. The optimumcomposition of PtNPs/PEDOT 0.3SG0.7as the modiﬁer of GCE for HER showed more acceptable results; i.e., lower overpotential,higher reduction current, and lower charge transfer resis-tance. This HER electrocatalyst electrochemically generateshydrogen as a stable and efﬁcient manner even after applying500th scan of potential without any loss of the current. TheHER mechanism of Heyrovsky for this electrocatalyst wasveriﬁed by the obtained Tafel equation and EIS results. Finally,the prepared nanocomposites, owing to its low overpotential, high long-term durability and efﬁciencies can recommend as the electrocatalyst for feasible HER. references [1]Nicoletti G, Arcuri N, Nicoletti G, Bruno R. A technical and environmental comparison between hydrogen and somefossil fuels. Energy Convers Manag 2015;89:205 e13. [2]Adiya ZISG, Dupont V, Mahmud T. Effect of hydrocarbon fractions, N 2and CO 2in feed gas on hydrogen production using sorption enhanced steam reforming: thermodynamicanalysis. Int J Hydrogen Energy 2017;42:21704 e18. [3]Guo X, Liu S, Huang S. Single Ru atom supported on defective graphene for water splitting: DFT and microkinetic investigation. Int J Hydrogen Energy 2018;43:4880 e92. [4]Hosseini SE, Mazlan AW. Hydrogen production from renewable and sustainable energy resources: promising green energy Carrier for clean development. Renew SustainEnergy Rev 2016;57:850 e66. [5]Shaner MR, Atwater HA, Lewis NS, McFarland EW. A comparativ