24  photocatalytic H2 production. The composite was assembled by the Ti-MOF PCN-415(NH2), the COF TpPa, and PdTCPP [palladium(II) meso-tetra(4-carboxyphenyl)porphine] (Figure 5). Notably, the MTV-Ti-MOF/COF composites revealed an enhancement in the photocatalytic H2 evolution performance under visible-light, with a maximum H2 evolution rate of 13.98 mmol.g-1.h-1 (turnover frequency (TOF) = 227 h-1) with PdTCPP⸦PCN-415(NH2)/TpPa, which is considerably greater than PdTCP⸦PPCN-415(NH2) (0.21 mmol.g-1.h-1) and TpPa (6.51 mmol.g-1.h-1 ) [78]. Figure 5. Synthesis approach of the MTV-Ti-MOF/COF [78].  In another work, Song et al. proceeded to incorporate [Ir(ppy)2(dcbpy)]Cl (ppy = 2- phenylpyridine, dcbpy = 2,2′-bipyridine-5,5′-dicarboxylate) into the framework of the large pores titanium MOF Ti3-BPDC (BPDC = biphenyl- 4,4′-dicarboxylate) forming Ti3-BPDC-Ir. A turnover number of 6632 and a HER rate of 925 µmol.g-1.h-1 was obtained under visible light (Figure 6) [109].
