108  MeOH can be absorbed in this position as methoxy and can consume the photogenerated holes, quenching the PL signal, whereas the TEOA is not able to access this position, therefore the PL signal seems unperturbed. These experiments seem to confirm the results obtained through the DFT calculations. Finally, by using both computational modeling and experimental methods it was possible to confirm that the hydrogen evolution reaction on COK-47 presents different mechanisms depending on the energy of the source of irradiation (Figure 47.d). Figure 47. (a) Atomic projection of the partial DOS; (b) OH-trapping experiments under visible illumination; (c) OH-trapping experiments under UV light; and (d) Wavelength-dependent HER mechanism for COK-47 [105].
