www.advancedsciencenews.com www.small-journal.com Figure6. a–c)LSVpolarizationcurvesandd)cellvoltageachievedatdiﬀerentcurrentdensities(10,50,and100mAcm−2)fortheNC-Pt-4( −)ǀǀIrO2(+) andPt/C( −)ǀǀIrO2(+)electrolyzersduringOWSinvariouselectrolytes.e)Long-termstabilityassessmentoftheNC-Pt-4catalystduringOWSatacurrent density of 50 mA cm−2in various electrolytes. f) Schematic representation of the two-electrode system used for OWS. g) Comparison of the OWS performanceoftheNC-Pt-4( −)ǀǀIrO2(+)electrolyzerwithrecentlyreportedcatalystsinvariouselectrolytes. possibilityforrobustinteractionbetweentheintermediatesand active sites within the NC-Pt catalyst during the HER process. In addition, Figure 7fdemonstrates that the NC-Pt catalyst exhibited a broader range of total density of states (TDOS) near the Fermi level than those of the NC and Pt-C catalysts. This indicatesenhancedconductivityandchargetransfercapabilities oftheNC-Ptcatalyst,resultingfromthemodiﬁcationoftheNC electronic structure through the incorporation of Pt, thereby enhancing the electrocatalytic activity for HER. Generally, the adsorption free energy of H*(ΔH*) was a crucial determinant fortheHERactivityofcatalysts.Whenthe ΔH*valuewascloser to zero, optimal hydrogen adsorption and desorption processes wereachieved.AsshowninFigure 7g,thecalculated ΔH*values for the NC, NC-Pt, and Pt-C catalysts were −0.68,−0.11, and −0.24eV,respectively.Theseﬁndingsrevealthatthe ΔH*valueoftheNC-PtcatalystwasnearlyzerocomparedtothoseoftheNC and Pt-C catalysts. Overall, the DFT results demonstrated that theincorporationofPtintotheNCmatrixcouldeﬀectivelymod- ulate the electronic structure, thereby signiﬁcantly improving the thermodynamic eﬃciency of hydrogen adsorption behavior andenhancingtheHERperformanceoftheNC-Ptcatalyst. 3.Conclusion Insummary,thepresentstudydemonstratedthesuccessfulde- sign of a self-supported NC matrix decorated with low-loading Pt nanoclusters, resulting in highly eﬀective electrocatalysts for HERinalkalineandalkalineseawaterelectrolytes.First,theNC matrixwassynthesizedfromZIF-8throughaPLAL-assistedtech- nique,followedbyhigh-temperaturepyrolysis.Subsequently,the Small2024,20,2403314 ©2024Wiley-VCHGmbH 2403314(11of14) 16136829, 2024, 40, Downloaded from https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/smll.202403314 by Beijing University of Chemistry Technology, Wiley Online Library on [28/03/2026]. See the Terms and Conditions (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/terms-and-conditions) on Wiley Online Library for rules of use; OA articles are governed by the applicable Creative Commons License
