www.advancedsciencenews.com www.small-journal.com Figure7. a)DFToptimizedcrystalstructuresoftheNC,NC-Pt,andPt–Ccatalysts(gray,violet,andbluespheresrepresentC,N,andPtatoms,respec- tively);b)localizedchargedensitydistributionoftheNC-Ptcatalyst.ThecalculatedPDOSforthec)NCcatalyst,d)NC-Ptcatalyst,ande)Pt–Ccat alyst. f)TDOScalculatedfortheNC,NC-Pt,andPt–Ccatalysts.g)GibbsfreeenergyplotsfortheHERprocessfortheNC,NC-Pt,andPt–Ccatalysts. NC-Pt catalyst was successfully decorated on the surface of the NC matrix via a PLIL reduction approach. Moreover, the elec- trocatalytic performanceoftheNC-Ptcatalysts was assessed for HER in alkaline and alkaline seawater electrolytes. The electro- chemical results conﬁrmed that the as-synthesized NC-Pt-4 cat- alystdemonstratedexcellentHERcatalyticperformance,includ- inglowoverpotential,asmallTafelslope,reducedchargetransfer resistance,highMA,alargerECSA,andremarkablestabilityin alkaline, simulated seawater, and alkaline seawater electrolytes, compared to commercial Pt/C. Meanwhile, the stability tests of the NC-Pt-4 catalyst revealed that its structural, morphological, and chemical composition remained unchanged before and af- terthestabilitytest.Inatwo-electrodesystemcomprisingNC-Pt- 4(−)ǀǀIrO2(+), we showed outstanding eﬃciency in alkaline sea- water electrolysis, requiring cell voltage of only 1.63 V to reach 10mAcm−2coupledwithexcellentstability.TheexcellentHER performanceandlong-termstabilityoftheNC-Pt-4catalystcouldbe attributed to its abundance of active sites, high surface area, N-richcarbon,excellentelectricalconductivity,andthesynergis- tic interaction between Pt nanoclusters and the NC matrix to provide an outstanding intrinsic catalytic performance. Accord- ingly,thedesignedNC-Pt-4catalystsdemonstratedsuperiorper- formanceinalkalineandalkalineseawater forHERandoverall waterelectrolysis,surpassingpreviouslyreportedcatalysts.This studypresentsauniqueandsimpletechniquefordesigningin- expensiveandhighlyeﬃcientelectrocatalystsforhydrogengen- erationinalkalineandalkalineseawaterenvironments. 4.ExperimentalSection Materials and Chemicals :Zinc plate (Zn, 99.99%), commercial Pt/C (20 wt% Platinum on carbon black), and 2-methylimidazole (C4H6N2, 97%) were purchased from Alfa Aesar, USA. Potassium tetrachloroplatinate(II) (K2PtCl4, 99%) and 5 wt% Naﬁon were obtained Small2024,20,2403314 ©2024Wiley-VCHGmbH 2403314(12of14) 16136829, 2024, 40, Downloaded from https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/smll.202403314 by Beijing University of Chemistry Technology, Wiley Online Library on [28/03/2026]. See the Terms and Conditions (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/terms-and-conditions) on Wiley Online Library for rules of use; OA articles are governed by the applicable Creative Commons License
