www.advancedsciencenews.com www.small-journal.com fromSigma–Aldrich,USA.Commercialiridiumoxide(IrO2,99.99%)was suppliedbyThermoScientiﬁc,USA.Ethylalcohol(C2H5OH,HPLCgrade, 99.9%) and potassium hydroxide (KOH, extra pure ﬂakes, 93%) were bought from Daejung Chemicals, South Korea. These chemicals were usedwithoutanyextrapuriﬁcationsteps. Synthesis of ZIF-8 Polyhedrons :The ZIF-8 polyhedron sample was synthesized via a PLAL process using a well-cleaned Zn plate and 2- methylimidazole. PLAL was conducted using a monochromatic laser (Nd:YAG, Surelite-II, pulse duration =7 ns, wavelength =1064 nm, and pulserepetitionrate =10Hz)withapulsepowerof100mJ,andthedis- tancebetweentheZnplateandfocuslenswas3cm.Indetail,aZnmetal platewasimmersedina20-mLglassvialcontaining10mLof1.0mKOH aqueous solution with well-dispersed 1.0 m 2-methylimidazole. The Zn metalplatewasablatedusingafocusedlaserbeamfor10mintogenerate nanosizedZnparticlesandZnionswithinaplasmaplume.TheseZnions furtherreactedwiththesolutionmixtureof2-methylimidazole,leadingto the formation of a white colloidal solution of ZIF-8 polyhedrons. Subse- quently,thiswhitecolloidalsolutionofZIF-8polyhedronswascentrifuged and rinsed with distilled water and ethyl alcohol to eliminate impurities. Finally,thecollectedZIF-8polyhedronsamplesweredriedat60 °Cfor12h. Synthesis of NC matrix :The N-doped carbon (NC) was synthesized usingdirectcarbonizationapproach.TheZIF-8polyhedronswerecalcined inatubefurnaceat900 °Cfor3hunderaN2gasﬂow.Subsequently,the tube furnace was allowed to cool naturally to room temperature (25 °C), andtheresultingNCsamplewastakenandwashedwithethylalcoholto removesurfacemoistureanddriedat60 °Cfor12h. Synthesis of NC-Pt catalyst :NC-Pt catalyst was synthesized through a PLIL process. In this detailed synthesis process, 2 mg of NC material was dispersed in a 5-mL glass vial with 2 mL of deionized water con- taining diﬀerent amounts of K2PtCl4, including 0.005, 0.01, 0.015, and 0.02 mmol. The reaction mixture was then irradiated with an unfocused laserbeamfromthepulsedlaser(Nd:YAG, Surelite-II-10)ona rotational diskfor5min.Theoptimalconditionsforthepulsedlaserincludedapulse powerof90mJ,apulserepetitionrateof10Hz,apulsedurationof7ns,a wavelengthof1064nm,anda5cmdistancebetweenthereactionmixture andthelaser.FollowingthePLILprocess,theresultingsolutionwascen- trifuged, thoroughly washed several times with ethyl alcohol to eliminate unreacted material, and dried at 60 °C for 12 h. Hereafter, the NC ma- terials decorated with Pt derived from the use of 0.005, 0.01, 0.015, and 0.02 mmol of K2PtCl4were denoted as NC-Pt-1, NC-Pt-2, NC-Pt-3, and NC-Pt-4,respectively. SupportingInformation SupportingInformationisavailablefromtheWileyOnlineLibraryorfrom theauthor. Acknowledgements V.M. and A.M. contributed equally to this work. This research was sup- ported by the Korea Basic Science Institute (National Research Facilities and Equipment Center) grant funded by the Ministry of Education (No. 2019R1A6C1010042).Theauthorsacknowledgetheﬁnancialsupportfrom the National Research Foundation of Korea (NRF) (2022R1A2C2010686, 2022R1A4A3033528,and2021R1C1C2010726). ConﬂictofInterest Theauthorsdeclarenoconﬂictofinterest. DataAvailabilityStatement The data that support the ﬁndings of this study are available from the correspondingauthoruponreasonablerequest.Keywords hydrogen evaluation reaction, N-doped carbon, Pt nanoclusters, pulsed laserablation,seawaterelectrolysis Received:April24,2024 Revised:August1,2024 Publishedonline:August17,2024 [1] A.Begum,M.Bose,G.Moula, Sci.Rep.2019,9,17027. [2] Q. He, D. Tian, H. Jiang, D. Cao, S. Wei, D. Liu, P. Song, Y. Lin, L. Song,Adv.Mater. 2020,32,1906972. [3] G.Wu,X.Han,J.Cai,P.Yin,P.Cui,X.Zheng,H.Li,C.Chen,G.Wang, X.Hong, Nat.Commun. 2022,13,4200. [4] J.Theerthagiri,S.J.Lee,A.P.Murthy,J.Madhavan,M.Y.Choi, Curr. Opin.SolidStateMater.Sci. 2020,24,100805. [5] Y .Y an,B.Xia,Z.Xu,X.W ang, ACSCatal. 2014,4,1693. [6] R. A. Senthil, S. Jung, A. Min, C. J. Moon, M. Y. Ch