inthe Nb 6octahedron, the centre site doped cluster is expected to have a poor CE. In contrast, the CEs of the centre site dopedclusters are higher than that of the pristine cluster due to strongbinding between the M and Nb atoms. The calculated d Nb–Ibond distance in the doped cluster is shorter than the pristine one,showing a stronger binding between the Nb and I atoms in thedoped clusters. For all the endohedrally doped clusters, we have calculated the vibrational freque ncies for the gamma point. All the frequencies are found to be positive with negligibly small imagin- ary (less than 1 meV) modes in the acoustic modes of a few clustersdue to the numerical noise. This confirms the dynamical stabilityof the clusters. These metal inserted clusters can be preparedusing a solid-state reaction with a high I atom concentration athigh temperatures, as suggested in different experiments on Coand Mn inserted Zr 6clusters.33,35,36 3.3 Thermodynamic stability of endohedrally doped MNb 6I18 clusters S i n c ew ea r ei n t e r e s t e di nt h ec e n t r es i t ed o p e dc a s e ,w eh a v e plotted their CE values against the elemental radius of the Matoms ( R M) depicted in Fig. 2(b) to understand the role of the size of central atoms. Here, RMis the theoretically estimated elemental radius taken from ref. 68. From this plot, it is clear that the CE ofthe centre site configuration increases as the R Mdecreases with slight variations, which come fr om electronic eﬀects in the ele- mental form of M atoms. For example, Cr and Mn have a lower CEthan expected due to the extra stability gained by the half-filled dorbitals in their atomic form. The atomic energies of all the Matoms are plotted in Fig. S3 (ESI †). After reaching a maximum CE for Co, it slightly decreases for Ni. It suddenly drops to a minimalvalue for Cu and Zn due to fewer unpaired electrons in their outerorbitals. In conclusion, the two critical factors that play a huge rolein influencing the stability of the centre site configuration are the R M, which leads to structural strain, and the number of unpaired electrons, whic h decide the Nb–M bond strength. 3.4 Formation stability of endohedrally doped MNb 6I18 clusters The insight from CE calculations proves that the centre site configuration is more stable for many metals. However, it isalso essential to show the conditions when such endohedrally Fig. 2 (a) CE of first-row M atoms (M = Sc to Zn) doped at the centre site and 3f-site of MNb 6I18clusters, and (b) CE of the centre site configuration of MNb 6I18clusters plotted against the atomic radii of the M atoms ( R) in Å. The dotted line in (a) shows the CE of the pristine Nb 6I18cluster, and the insets show the M atom doped cluster configurations at the 3f-site and centre site. The blue-coloured balls show the M atoms.Paper PCCP Published on 08 April 2025. Downloaded by Beijing University of Chemical Technology on 4/15/2026 1:43:35 AM. View Article Online
