Chemical Engineering Journal 433 (2022) 134571 3the morphologies of the as-prepared alloys with different compositions (see Figure S2). However, all alloys can form nanoporous structures with continuous nanopore and nanosheet/nanofollower morphologies. Fig. 2c-i displays the HRTEM image, SAED image, HAADF-STEM image and EDX mapping of the 1-PtNiMg-900 alloy. As shown in Fig. 2c, the interplanar spacings of 0.206 nm and 0.175 nm of the nanaporous 1- PtNiMg-900 alloy correspond to the (111) and (200) facets of the cubic metallic Ni structure. The selected area diffraction pattern (SAED) in Fig. 2d displays multicrystalline diffraction rings indexing to the (111), (200) and (220) facets of Ni solid solution, which is consistent with the XRD analysis. The EDX elemental mapping in Fig. 2f-i shows that Ni, Pt, Mg and O atoms were homogeneously dispersed in the nanoporous alloy bulk. Fig. 3 displays the XPS spectra of the 1-PtNiMg-900 alloy before and after ageing. The full survey spectra explicitly confirm the existence of Ni, Pt, Mg and O species in the inner and outer surfaces of the 1-PtNiMg- 900 alloy (see Figure S3). Fig. 3a shows the Pt 4f spectrum of the 1- PtNiMg-900 alloy before and after ageing. Two chemically different Pt species are ascertained by fitting the Pt 4f spectra of unaged and aged samples. For the XPS spectrum of the unaged 1-PtNiMg-900 alloy, the peaks of Pt 4f7/2 and 4f5/2 located at 70.8 eV and 74.1 eV can be ascribed to the signals of Pt0, and the bonding energy of Pt 4f7/2 (Pt 4f5/2) collected at 71.93 eV (75.19 eV) corresponds to Pt2. After ageing, the bonding energies of Pt 4f7/2 (Pt 4f5/2) observed at 71.11 eV (74.47 eV) and 72.38 eV (75.45 eV) correspond to the Pt0and Pt2species, respectively. Obviously, the bonding energies of Pt 4f of the aged sample have an increase of approximately 0.4 eV compared to the unaged sample, indicating a change in the density of electronic states of the Pt species during the HER process. In addition, Ni 3p peaks are also observed in the Pt 4f spectrum. The change in the Ni 3p signal after 1- Fig. 2.(a, b) FESEM images of the 1-PtNiMg-900 alloy at different magnifications. (c) HRTEM, (d) SAED and (e) HAADF-STEM images of the 1-PtNiMg-900 alloy before ageing. EDX mappings of (f) Pt, (g) Ni, (h) Mg and (i) O in the 1-PtNiMg-900 alloy before ageing. Y. Zheng et al.
