Chemical Engineering Journal 433 (2022) 134571 5conductivity. The Tafel slope has been widely employed to study the reaction ki- netics mechanism of electrocatalyst materials for water splitting. Currently, there are the two HER paths of Volmer-Tafel and Volmer- Heyrovsky, which can be divided into the three modes of Volmer (RDS)-Heyrovsky (or Tafel), Volmer-Heyrovsky (RDS) and Volmer-Tafel (RDS) according to different rate-determining steps (RDS), resulting in three Tafel slopes of 118 mV dec-1, 39 mV dec-1 and 30 mV dec-1, respectively [47-52] . Fig. 4b shows the iRs-corrected Tafel plots of all as- prepared electrodes originating from the LSV curves in Fig. 4a. As shown in the figure, the 1-PtNiMg-900 alloy electrode exhibits a Tafel slope of (30.9 mV dec-1), lower than 0.05-PtNiMg-900 (120.7 mV dec-1), 0.1- PtNiMg-900 (64.5 mV dec-1), 0.3-PtNiMg-900 (31.0 mV dec-1), 0.5- PtNiMg-900 (34.3 mV dec-1), 3-PtNiMg-900 (31.1 mV dec-1) and 5- PtNiMg-900 (34.9 mV dec-1), further confirming the Volmer-Tafel mechanism for the HER in an alkaline medium and the superior elec- trocatalytic activity. To thoroughly examine the HER kinetics, EIS is employed to analyse the charge-transfer resistance of all as-prepared Fig. 4.Electrocatalytic measurements: (a) 0.05-PtNiMg-900, 0.1-PtNiMg-900, 0.3-PtNiMg-900, 0.5-PtNiMg-900,1-PtNiMg-900,3-PtNiMg-900 and 5-PtNiMg-900 alloys and commercial Pt/C electrodes in a 1 M KOH solution. (b) The iRs-corrected Tafel plots of all as-prepared electrodes are derived from the curves of Fig. 4a. (c) Nyquist plots of all as-prepared electrodes measured at an HER voltage of 47 mV (vs. RHE) over a frequency range of 100000 –0.01 Hz in a 1 M KOH solution. The inset shows the plots in the high-frequency region. (d) Cdl values of all as-prepared electrodes measured in a 1 M KOH solution. (e) Multicurrent step experiment of all the electrodes performed in a 1 M KOH solution at different constant current densities of 1, 10, 50, 100 and 200 mA cm␀2. (f) LSV curves of the 1- PtNiMg-900 alloy electrode before and after the ageing test for 100 h at a current density of 2000 mA cm␀2 in a two-electrode cell. Y. Zheng et al.
