Ceramics International 49 (2023) 1020–1029 Available online 11 September 2022 0272-8842/© 2022 Elsevier Ltd and Techna Group S.r.l. All rights reserved.Fatigue free relaxor ferroelectric and electrocatalytic hydrogen evolution of yttrium substituted BaBi 2Nb2O9 layered structured nanoceramics for energy storage application Mrinal Kanti Adaka,b, Debasish Mondala, Ranadhir Samantaa, Biswarup Chakrabortyb, Debasis Dhaka,* aDepartment of Chemistry, Sidho-Kanho-Birsha University, Purulia, 723104, India bDepartment of Chemistry, Indian Institute of Technology Delhi, Hauz Khas, New Delhi, 110016, India ARTICLE INFO Keywords: Relaxor ferroelectrics Nanomaterials Solid-state synthesis Slim hysteresis Hydrogen evolution reaction BaBi 2Nb2O9 ABSTRACT Lead-free bismuth layered structured ferroelectric ceramics are highly important in superior energy storage applications. The slim hysteresis curve with high energy storage density and efficiency is expected for wide application. In this regard, the suitable electrocatalyst for the generation of hydrogen gas through water-splitting show high importance as an alternative energy source. The current article aims to investigate the above goals by incorporating 5% yttrium at the place of bismuth for BaBi 2Nb2O9 relaxor ferroelectrics. The solid-state syn- thesized method successfully prepared the single-phase material and is confirmed through spectroscopic and morphological analysis. The dielectric characteristics follow diffused phase transition with broad temperature dependence that indicated the space charge polarization in the material owing to the presence of Y3at different domains. The higher degree of diffuseness and low dielectric loss implies the significant role of charge carriers during frequency and temperature variation in the dielectric study. Impedance spectroscopy analysis indicates the non-Debye type relaxation and NTCR behavior of the material that is correlated to the multiple relaxation processes. The slim P-E hysteresis curve and fatigue-free properties of the materials up to 106 cycles reflect its usefulness in the potential device as NVRAM applications. The materials are also used for hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) under an electrochemical condition. A lower overpotential value of 180 mV is obtained at 10 mA cm␀2 current density. The lower Tafel slope and charge transfer resistance value support its superior HER ac- tivity. The above results demonstrated the potential application of the studied material (BaBi 1⋅9Y0⋅1Nb2O9) in the energy storage application and as an electrocatalyst for alternative energy source. 1.Introduction Ferroelectric materials have spontaneous polarization which can be reoriented between corresponding domain states by an applied electric field. It is also well known that the polarization of ferroelectrics affects the electrical behavior of charge carriers. Like ferroelectricity, hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) is also a method of energy conversion and energy storage, a means to replace the traditional fossil fuels [1,2]. Aurivillius structured ceramics or bismuth layered structured ferro- electric ceramics (BLSFs) show great effort for the use in nonvolatile ferroelectric random-access memory (NVFRAM) and high-temperature applications [3–5]. A lot of attention of BLSFs to the scientific commu - nity is due to their unique characteristics like high Curie point, good thermal stability, and improved polarization with fatigue-free nature [6, 7]. Shape-dependent properties of the BLSFs and the creation of defects through ionizing or displacement effect attract the scientific community highly. This type of distortion leads to the formation of the local electric field through interstitial defects [8]. This lead-free ceramic is also desirable as an alternative to lead zirconium titanate owing to the rise of environmental concerns. (Bi2O2)2(Am-1BmO3m1)2- is the general for- mula of BLSFs, where (Bi2O2)2layers and [BO 6] octahedrons are alternatively stacked along the c-axis. Here, 12 coordinated A-site is occupied by mono-, di-, or trivalent ion, octahedral coordinated B-site is occupied by tri-, tetra-, penta-, or hexavalent ion, and m (varies from 1 to 6) indicates the number of [BO 6] octahedra in pseudo-perovskite slabs [9–11]. The structural feature of BLSFs leads to the restriction of *Corresponding author. E-mail address: debasisdhak@gmail.com (D. Dhak). Contents lists available at ScienceDirect Ceramics International u{�~zkw! s{yo|kr o>!ÐÐÐ1ow�o �to~1m{y2w{m k�o2mo~kyt z�! https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ceramint.2022.09.077 Received 27 July 2022; Received in revised form 1 September 2022; Accepted 6 September 2022
