4 [39] were reported using BCME. In such investigatio ns, the synthesis in BCME mainly led to 1 spherical nanoparticles as random agglomerates. How ever, the preparation of inorganic 3D 2 hierarchical superstructures using BCME as confined  reaction media has not been explored so 3 far. The closest situation is when a monolithic, po lymerized BCME is infiltrated with inorganic 4 precursors such as tetraethyl orthosilicate (TEOS) into its porous network, followed by 5 calcination [40]. However, such approach has only b een applied to the preparation of certain 6 materials such as bicontinuous SiO 2 and normally the characteristic dimensions of poly meric 7 BCME are larger than that of conventional BCME.  8 The channels of BCME have a thickness in the order of tens of nanometers. Both water and oil 9 channels are continuous phases, having infinite len gths. Thus, it is feasible to imagine the growth 10 of hierarchical superstructures inside them, as the  narrow thickness of the channels will allow the 11 formation of nanometric building blocks, whilst the ir interconnection will allow the self- 12 assembly of these nanoparticles into 3D networks. T his is, to the best of our knowledge, the first 13 report on the synthesis of platinum hierarchical su perstructures (PtHSs), and in general metallic 14 HSs, in bicontinuous microemulsion media using lipo philic and hydrophilic platinum salts as the 15 starting material. The crystalline structure, morph ology, size of the novel PtHSs and the 16 electrocatalytic activity towards HER were fully ev aluated.  17 2. Materials and methods 18 2.1. Chemicals 19 (1,5-cyclooctadiene) dimethylplatinum( Ⅱ) 97% (C 10 H16 Pt, Pt-COD), Chloroplatinic acid 20 hexahydrate ≥ 37.50% (H 2PtCl 6. 6H 2O), Isooctane 99% (C 8H18 ), Sodium borohydride 99.99% 21 (NaBH 4), Nafion 5 wt %, were purchased from Sigma Aldrich . Synperonic TM  91/5 (C 19 O6H40 ) 22 was purchased from CRODA. Nitric acid 69.3 % (HNO 3), Isopropyl alcohol 99.9 % (C 3H8O) 23 were supplied by Fisher Scientific, Sulphuric acid H 2SO 4 (93-98%) was purchased from 24 Fermont.  25 2.2. Formulation of bicontinuous microemulsion and synthesis of Pt hierarchical superstructures 26 (PtHSs) 27 The preparation of BCME was carried out in 20 mL gl ass vials. The proper amount of (1,5- 28 cyclooctadiene) dimethyl platinum( Ⅱ) (Pt-COD) was weighed and dissolved in isooctane t o give 29
