14 In order to elucidate the reaction mechanism involv ed as well as identifying the rate-limiting step 1 in the HER by the PtHSs electrocatalysts, Tafel plo ts were constructed [65]. It has been widely 2 reported that, in acidic electrolytes, the mechanis m involved in hydrogen production through 3 HER [18, 66], involves a two-step process. The init ial step (rate determining step) is the Volmer 4 reaction (H 3O+ + e -  Hads  + H 2O [discharge step]). In the Volmer reaction, the su rface of the 5 working electrode adsorbs a proton from the acidic solution and forms an adsorbed hydrogen 6 atom [67]. The next step is helpful in the desorpti on of the reactive intermediate H ads  either by 7 Tafel reaction (2H ads   H2 [recombination step]) or Heyrovsky reaction (H 3O+ + e - + H ads  H2 + 8 H2O [electrodesorption step]). Each mechanism can be related to a given value of the slope 9 obtained from the Tafel equation  = a + b log j, where  is the overpotential (V), j is the 10 normalized current density (mA cm -2), a is the intercept and b is the Tafel slope (mV dec -1). 11 Slope values close to 30, 40 and 120 mV dec -1 represent Tafel, Heyrovsky and Volmer steps 12 respectively. A slope value of 30 mV dec -1 translates to Volmer-Tafel mechanism which 13 suggests coupled discharge-electrodeposition proces s and at 40 mV dec -1, Volmer-Heyrovsky 14 mechanism, which implies coupled discharge-chemical  desorption. 15 Table 2:  Comparison of the electrochemical parameter measur ed for different Pt and Pt-based 16 electrocatalysts with the PtHSs investigated in thi s work 17 Electrocatalyst  Tafel slope mV dec -1 Electrolyte  ECSA m2/g n Rct  Ω η10  /mV Ref Pt/C  34 0.5 M H2SΟ4 - - - 62  [67] Pt -Cu/CNFs - 1:2 68  0.5 M H2SO 4 - - - 71  [68] AuPt NC  41  0.5 M H2SO 4 21.76   - 32  [69] Pt/MoS2/SSM  42.7  0.5 M H2SO 4 - - - 87  [70] Pt@NOMC - 700 88  0.5 M H2SO 4  - - 90  [71] Pt -Ag/SiNW - 2 70  0.5 M H2SO 4 - - - 13 5 [72] Pt -CNSs/RGO  29  0.5 M H2SO 4 23.4  - 55  - [73] Pt