19 and interface. The morphology showed that the resul ting material had a unique interconnected 1 and continuous arrangements between each consecutiv e nanomaterials. Each nanomaterial 2 exhibits a spherical shape. This led to the hierarc hical nature of the PtH-O (Fig. 2 a – b).  3 4 5 Scheme 1: Illustration of the progressive formation  of Platinum nanostructures in BC-ME 6 reaction method using Oil soluble precursor. 7 8 Equation 2: Chemical reaction between chloroplatini c acid and sodium borohydride [83] 9 10 Scheme 2: Illustration of the progressive formation  of Platinum nanostructures in BC-ME 11 reaction method using water soluble precusor. 12 Considering the composition of the bicontinuous mic roemulsions from this study, 20.64 % 13 aqueous phase, 27.36 % Synperonic TM 91/5 and 52 % Isooctane, it is feasible to imagine that the 14 water channels must be narrower than the oil channe ls. In addition, Synperonic® 91/5, being a 15 nonionic surfactant with 5 EO units, has the abilit y to become highly hydrated. According to 16 Garti et al. and other authors, nonionic surfactant s can bound up to 3 water molecules per EO 17 unit in similar ternary or pseudoternary systems [8 4]. In fact, according to the BCME 18 composition used, our microemulsions have an H 2O : EO molar ratio around 3 (3.03 for PtH-A2, 19 2.9 for PtH-A4, and 3.2 for PtH-O). This means that  all the water present in the microemulsions 20 must be bound to the EO units from the nonionic sur factant.  Which implies that not only must 21 the water channels be narrower than the oil channel s, but also, the water inside the channels must 22 be more restricted, more structured as compared to molecules in the oil channels, because the 23 presence of “free” water is unlikely. The metal ion s from the precursors, are also more restricted 24 as compared to the situation where the precursor is  in the oil phase.  25 The restriction imposed by the bound water in the B CME channels leads to the formation of a 26 favoured arrangement, where the primary particles a re smaller and the surface area is larger, as 27
