20 compared to the situation when oil-soluble precurso rs are used. Thus, we can conclude that 1 synthesis of Pt nanostructures in our nonionic bico ntinuous microemulsion system leads to a 2 template effect when the water-soluble precursors a re used. Which is not the case when ionic 3 surfactant-based microemulsions (AOT, CTAB based) a re used, as isolated or randomly 4 agglomerated spherical particles are obtained [39, 85]. Furthermore, as opposed to other 5 inorganic hierarchical superstructures synthesized using BCME, there is no need for templating 6 with a polymerized oil phase followed by impregnati on and calcination to remove the template 7 [40]. On the contrary, our approach is one-pot, sof t, there is no need for any special equipment, 8 and the liquid BCME template is removed simply by w ashings with conventional solvents 9 including water.  10 11 4. Conclusion 12 In this study, we synthesized platinum hierarchical  superstructures (PtHSs) in bicontinuous 13 microemulsion reaction medium (BCME). This was achi eved using two different precursors 14 based on their solubility preferences. It was obser ved that PtHSs fabricated using lipophilic and 15 hydrophilic platinum precursor exhibited different morphologies, namely 3D mesh and 16 nanocoral shape. SEM, EDX, HRTEM, XRD, and electroc hemical techniques were used to study 17 the morphological variations, crystallinity and ele ctrocatalytic properties of PtHSs. The 18 crystalline platinum superstructures were connected  together in a manner directed by the 19 interconnected network structure of BCME, demonstra ting for the first time the template effect 20 for the direct synthesis of metallic materials in B CME. The electrochemical functionality of the 21 PtH-A2 showed a higher activity than PtH-A4 and PtH -O. A Tafel slope of 30 mV dec -1 was 22 recorded for PtH-A2, indicating that Volmer-Tafel m echanism was observed in the HER. The 23 PtHSs were stable over a long polarization of 1000 cycles. In general, the hydrophilic platinum 24 precursor exhibited better performance. It is there fore promising to know that these unique 25 structures synthesized by BCME facilitate the plati num properties that are of technological 26 importance as novel catalysts and electrocatalysts.  27 Acknowledgments 28
