lytocarbonsupportswithoutnitrogen dopingofferanearlyidealpathwayforthehydrogenevolution reaction(HER),especiallycomparedtopathwaysonN-doped carbonsupports.4Despitetheapparentadvantages ofthis structuralmotif,thelimitedmethodologies availableforthe synthesisofSAcatalystshavehinderedthefullrealizationof thisstrategy. ■RESULTSANDDISCUSSION PtSAsweresynthesized viaelectrochemical depositiononto porouscarbonsupportsfromanaqueoussolutioncontaininga lowconcentration (0.4mM)ofH2PtCl6atpH10byapplyingapotentialof−0.8VvsAg/AgCl(firstpotentialsweeponly; FigureS1A).5High-resolution transmission electronmicros- copy(HR-TEM) analysisconfirmedtheisolatedatomic distribution ofPtontheporouscarbonsupport,asevidenced byfaintspotsinbright-field(BF)-TEMandclearbrightspots indarkfield(DF)-TEM images(Figure1a,b).Incontrast, usinghigherconcentrations ofPtprecursorandlowerpH conditionsresultedinPtnanoclusters (NCs)oflessthan1nm (0.6mM,twoscansrepeated)andnanoparticles (NPs)larger than3nm(3mM,threescansrepeated)atthesame electrochemical potential(FiguresS1BandS2). Thedeposition mechanism wasdrivenprimarilyby variationsinprecursorconcentration, solutionpH,and resultingelectrostatic interactions atthecarboninterface (Figure1C).AthighpH(pH10)andarelativelylow precursorconcentration, theporouscarbonsurfaceacquiresa negativecharge,limitingtheaccumulation ofnegatively chargedPt(OH)62−complexesintheSternlayerdueto electrostatic repulsion.6Additionally, theelectricdoublelayer exhibitsanextendedbutsparsedistribution ofprecursor anionsneartheinterface,attributedtothelowproton concentration intheelectrolyte. Uponapplyingabrief Received: July18,2025 Revised: August14,2025 Accepted: August15,2025 Published: August28,2025 Article pubs.acs.org/JACS ©2025American Chemical Society 33281https://doi.org/10.1021/jacs.5c12309 J.Am.Chem.Soc.2025,147,33281−33287 Downloaded via BEIJING UNIV OF CHEMICAL TECHNOLOGY on March 30, 2026 at 01:21:40 (UTC). See https://pubs.acs.org/sharingguidelines for options on how to le