ions, PtNPs interactcooperatively withhydroxylradicals(OH•)generated fromwaterdissociation atneighboring catalyticsites,23 facilitatingtheelectrochemical oxidationofadsorbedCO intoCO2.21ThismechanismparallelsthatofPtSAssupported onN-dopedcarbon,wherethesupportparticipates asa cocatalystduringthewateroxidationprocess.19Thisenablesa cooperative mechanism similartothatobservedinPtNPs, thusrequiringafundamentally differentinterpretation forthe behaviorofPtSAs.Conversely, PtSAselectrochemically depositedonpurecarbonsupportslackadjacentactivesites capableofsupportingCOoxidationthroughwaterdissocia- tion.Thisexplainswhy,inmanystudiesonSAcatalysts,the ECSAdetermined throughCOstrippinginacidicconditionsis lesscommonlyreported,withresearchers optinginsteadfor thequantification ofPtatomsviaICPanalysis(TableS1). However,theICPmethodisvalidonlywhenthesynthesized samplesarecomposedexclusivelyofPtSAs,withoutclusters orparticles.IncaseswheretheECSAdiffersfromthetotalPt contentduetoinaccessible siteswithinthestructure,ICP analysismayyieldaninaccurateestimate(overestimate) of accessiblePtcontent.Asdemonstrated here,PtSAsinalkaline conditionbenefitfromtheabundantsupplyofOH−ions, facilitatingCO2conversionduringCOstrippingexperiments. Thisprovidesaneffectiveapproachtoback-calculate thenumberofactivePtSAs,therebyofferingmoreaccurate assessments ofcatalystperformance. Infuturesingle-atom catalystdesign,werecognizethateven subtleinteractions betweenasingleatomanditssupportcan readilyaltertheatom’sintrinsicproperties.Therefore,adesign approachthatexplicitlyaccountsforsuchelectronic perturbations isessential.Forexample,onecouldconsider elementspositionedslightlyoffthevolcanoplotapex�other thanPt�andtailorthesupportinteractions toshifttheir hydrogenbindingenergybacktowardtheoptimum.Thisis inherentlycomplexandchallenging, requiringcarefulcontrol overstructuralandelectronicfactors.Leveraging AI-driven screening,inconjunction withDFT-based two-dimensional mapping24approaches thatcapturetheseintricatestructural interactions, couldgreatlyacceleratethediscoveryofsuch optimalmaterial−support pairings. ■CONCLUSION Insummary,wesuccessfully synthesized preciselydefinedPt SAsonpurecarbonsupportthroughelectrochemical deposition, aimingtoadjustthecriteriaforSAcatalystsin HERandclarifythestructuralconcept.Theelectrochemically depositedPtSAcatalystdemonstrated exceptional catalytic performance in0.5MH2SO4electrolyte, achievingamass activityof287A·mg−1andaTOFof290s−1atan overpotential of50mV.Thisexceptional performance results fromtheintrinsicpropertiesofisolatedPtatoms,preserved withoutsignificantelectronicperturbation duetominimal supportinteractions, asconfirmed byDFTcalculations. AmongvariousexaminedPtSAconfigurations, thePt−C4- positionedPtatomexhibitedthemostfavorablehydrogen adsorption energies.Notably,itwasobservedthattwo hydrogenatomspreferentially adsorbsimultaneously onthe Pt−C4siteinanexothermic andspontaneous reaction. Moreover,underalkalineconditions(1MKOH),PtSAs displayeddistinctelectrochemical behavior,characterized bya higherHERoverpotential andlimitedwaterreduction capability,highlighting theirinherentcatalyticlimitationsfor waterdissociation. DFTcalculations supportthis,showinga highendothermic barrierof1.51eVforwaterreductionatPt− C4sites.Additionally, COstrippingexperiments inalkaline electrolyteconditionsconfirmedactivesiteaccessibility and catalyticefficacy,closelymatchingtheelectrochemical surface area(ECSA)measurements obtainedfromICPanalyses. Thesefindingsdecisivelydifferentiate theintrinsiccatalytic activityofPtSAsfromeffectsinducedbysupportinteractions, suggestingthatfutureresearchshouldstrategically optimize supportinteractions, possiblythroughtailoredheteroatom doping,tosimultaneously enhancecatalyticperformance and stability. ■ASSOCIATED CONTENT +sıSupporting Information TheSupporting Information isavailablefreeofchargeat https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/jacs.5c12309. Additionalexperimental detailsincludingsynthesisofPt SA,PtNC,andPtNPcat