rwettabilityforuniformgrowth,andasan electron-conductingpathfortheHERprocess.AdualTM-doped TMD electrocatalyst is simply prepared via a simple chalcoge- nization of a mixed liquid-phase precursor-coated TiOx/Ti sub- strate. Uniformly distributed V- and Co-doped ReS2are clearly distinguished in the transmission electron microscopy (TEM) image,whichisfacilitatedbytheuniqueﬂippeddiamond-shaped motif(DM)inCo-dopedReS2.TheHERcatalyticactivityshows low overpotentials of 31, 83, and 59 mV at a current density of 10mAcm−2inacidic, neutral,andalkalinemedia,respectively, with high cyclic durability. Density-functional theory (DFT) cal- culationsrevealthatthesharplyreducedenergybarrierforwater dissociation ΔGH2O(0.68 eV) and low hydrogen adsorption en- ergyΔGH*(0.15 eV) in the dual doping system of ReS2signiﬁ- cantly improve the hydrogen evolution process in alkaline elec- trolyte. 2.ResultsandDiscussion 2.1.UniversalGrowthPlatformforTMDs We devised a universal platform for directly growing dual TM- doped TMDs on a thermally oxidized Ti (TiOx/Ti) electrode for HER applications over a wide pH range ( Figure1a). Ti foils are thermally oxidized at 500 °C to form the native TiOxlayers andcoatedwithliquid-phaseprecursorscontainingamixtureofTM precursors(suchasNaReO4,C oCl2·6H2O,andVCl3inaqueous solution). Single TM- and dual TM-doped TMDs can be grown overtheentireTifoilsviasimplechalcogenizationunderS-rich conditions at elevated temperatures. The TiOxlayer functions as a chalcogen and TM diﬀusion barrier into the Ti bulk for surface-limitedreactionsandenhancesthewettabilityofprecur- sors for the uniform growth of TMDs. Furthermore, the elec- trical conductivity and wettability of TiOx/Ti are still compara- ble to that of bare Ti, enabling the direct use of the electrode forHER(Figure S1,SupportingInformation).Thephotographs of the bare substrate and subsequently oxidized TiOx/Ti, ReS2- grownTiOx/Ti,andV:Co-ReS2-grownTiOx/Tishowdiﬀerentcor- respondingcolors,buteachsurfacemorphologyimagedbyscan- ningelectronmicroscopy(SEM)appearsuniform(Figure 1band FigureS2, Supporting Information). Notably, when Ti foils are not oxidized, fragmented patched ReS2grows alongside TiS2 (FigureS2b,c,SupportingInformation).Thecharacteristicpeaks of the amorphous-like rutile phase near 440 ( Eg) and 610 cm−1 (A1g) in the Raman spectra appear in pristine and oxidized Ti foils, and all characteristic features of ReS2with low-frequency Eg-like modes at 136.8 and 144.5 cm−1are clearly observed in ReS2and V:Co-ReS2samples (Figure 1c).[30]Furthermore, the development of (100), (002), and (004) peaks of ReS2in the X- ray diﬀraction (XRD) spectra is observed in pristine and V:Co- ReS2,inadditiontotheXRDpeaksofTimetal(Figure 1d).The characteristic diﬀraction peaks of titanium oxides are not de- tected in any samples, indicating that a very thin layer of TiOx is present on top of the Ti surface.[31]The presence of the top- most ReS2layer and TiOxon Ti foils is conﬁrmed by a cross- sectional high-angle annular dark-ﬁeld scanning transmission electronmicroscopy(HAADF)-STEMandrelatedenergydisper- siveX-rayspectroscopy(EDS)mapping(Figure 1e). Notably, Re and S elements are only found on the surface of the native Ti oxide, demonstrating that the chemically inert Ti oxidelayermainlyservesasadiﬀusionbarrierforchalcogenand transition metal atoms, thereby enabling the surface-mediated wafer-scalegrowthofvariousTMDsontheTifoils(Figure S3a, Supporting Information). The highly crystalline layers of ReS2 can be clearly observed on top of the amorphous TiOxlayer/Ti foil (Figure 1fand Figure S3b,c, Supporting Information). We further conﬁrm that the TiOx/Ti foil can function as a growth platformforotherTMDs,includingMoS2,WS2,andWS e2,and can be directly used for electrocatalysis (Figure S4, Supporting Information). 2.2.StructuralAnalysisofTMDopedReS2 The crystal structures of pristine and TM-doped ReS2with sin- gleanddualdopants(VandCo)arecarefullyinvestigatedusing annular dark-ﬁeld scanning transmission electron microscopy (ADF-STEM). The schematic of a ball-and-stick model for dis- torted1T-ReS2inFigure2ashowsarhombicarrayofanin-plane DM that consists of four Re atoms. The DMs are closely linked alongthe[100]and[110]directions.ThedistortedReS2produces diﬀerent lattice parameters of a1≠b1and a2≠b2.T h ea t o m i c modeldescribesonlyReatomsbecausethecontrastintheADF imageisapproximatelyscaledtothesquareoftheatomicnumber Small2024,20,2308672 ©2023Wiley-VCHGmbH 2308672(2of11) 16136829, 2024, 22, Downloaded from https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/smll.202308672 by Beijing University of Chemistry Technology, Wiley Online Library on [30/03/2026]. See the Terms and Conditions (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/terms-and-conditions) on Wiley Online Library for rules of use; OA articles are governed by the applicable Creative Commons License
