www.advancedsciencenews.com www.small-journal.com TounderstandthechemicalinteractionofHandOHwithsur- face S atoms, we calculated the corresponding charge density diﬀerences as shown in Figure 4e–h. Notably, the HO-S bond becomes stronger with V and Co doping and is the strongest on V:Co-ReS2. In contrast, the H–S bonds remain virtually un- changedregardlessofdoping.TheincreasedHO–Sbondingby Co-V doping leads to more stable H +OH adsorption. Figure 4i shows the calculated free-energy diagrams for the HER process onthepristine,V-doped,Co-doped,andV:Co-ReS2andPt(111). FortheVolmer stepofwater dissociation, whichisusually con- sidered the critical step, pristine ReS2exhibits a high water dis- sociation barrier ( ΔGH2O: 3.25 eV), whereas those of V- and Co- doped ReS2(1.37 and 1.54 eV, respectively) are substantially re- duced. More importantly, V:Co-ReS2displays the lowest ΔGH2O of 0.68 eV, conﬁrming that water dissociation occurs more eas- ilyonthesurfaceofV:Co-ReS2comparedtothatonthePt(111) surface ( ΔGH2Oof 1.06 eV). It is worth noting that the aver- age percentage of coupled V:Co dopants in ReS2is 6.5%, as identiﬁedthroughADF-STEManalysis(Figure S24,Supporting Information). The signiﬁcantly low ΔGH2Oof V:Co-ReS2is associated with the strong HO–S bond conﬁrmed from the charge-density dif- ference(Figure 4h).Suchalowkineticbarrierforwaterdissocia- tionleadstorapidHsupply.ForH2generation,theHadsorption Gibbsfreeenergies( ΔGH*)ofV-,Co-,andV:Co-ReS2(0.17,0.45, and 0.15 eV, respectively) are much lower than 1.36 eV of the pristineReS2(Figure4iandTableS4,SupportingInformation). Therefore,dopingReS2withTMdopantssuchasVandCoisben- eﬁcialforthehydrogenevolutionprocess.Speciﬁcally,inthecase ofV:Co-ReS2,theoptimalselectivebindingsiteforthehydroxyl group (OH-) is more readily facilitated on the sulfur atom adja- centtotheVsite.Concurrently,thereleasedhydrogen(H+)isad- sorbedonthesulfuratomadjacenttotheCosite,enablingmore eﬃcienthydrogengeneration.Tounderstandthecharge-transfer kinetics, the partial density of states (PDOS) of TM-doped ReS2 isfurthercalculated(Figure 4j).WhilethepristineReS2exhibits a wide bandgap and zero DOS at the Fermi level, the introduc- tionofVandCodopantsgivesrisetonewelectronicstatesnear theFermilevel.SuchhybridizedelectronicstatesneartheFermi levelsigniﬁcantlyappearduetoV:Codualdoping,whichleadsto highchargeconcentrationandenhancedchargetransferduring HERprocesses.ThePDOSofSatomswhereHandOHadsorb clearlyshowsmixingwithVandCodopants,andconsequently, TMdopingaﬀectstheelectronicstateoftheSatomandtheinter- actionwithHandOH(Figure S25,SupportingInformation).It isimportanttonotethattheformationofﬂippedDM,facilitated bytheintroductionofCodopinginReS2,signiﬁcantlyinﬂuences theconductivityofV:Co-ReS2,whileVdopingenhancestheHER activity. The volcano plot is summarized with various 2D TMDs and metals in the literature (Figure 4k). Both Gibbs free energy and exchange current density of V:Co-ReS2are far superior to those of most reported 2D TMDs.[33]Figure4ldisplays the HER pro- cesswithV:Co-ReS2inhigherpHmedia.H2Omoleculesarepre- dominantlydissociatedatSsitesnearVatoms,andtheadsorbed protons diﬀuse to the active site (S sites near V and Co atoms), eventuallyresultinginH2evolution.2.5.AlkalineWaterElectrolyzerPerformance For industrial applications, we demonstrate an alkaline water electrolyzer with V:Co-ReS2. A highly porous Ti mesh is used as the electrode to increase the surface area. After the oxidiza- tion of the Ti mesh (see Experimental Section for details) and subsequentcoatingitwithprecursors,ﬂowershapedV:Co-ReS2 are grown ( Figure5a). The SEM images in Figure 5bshow the smoothandroughsurfacesofpristineTiandoxidizedTimeshes, respectively,andtheTEMimageshowsthesimilaratomicstruc- ture of V:Co-ReS2(FiguresS26,S27, Supporting Information). The coarse surface of oxidized Ti mesh induces the growth of ﬂower-shapeddualTM-dopedReS2.Weconstructedthealkaline waterelectrolyzerbycouplingtheV:Co-ReS2cathodewithaRuO2 anode in an aqueous KOH solution (photograph in Figure 5c). The water-splitting performance far exceeds that of an alkaline water electrolyzer prepared by pairing state-of-the-art RuO2and Pt/Ccatalysts.TheV:Co-ReS2||RuO2alkalinewaterelectrolyzer onlyneededanovervoltageof360mV(1.59Vcell),whichis80mV lower than that of the Pt/C || RuO2(1.67 Vcell) for a cell current density of 10 mA cm−2(Figure5d,e). The cell voltage was su- perior to those of most recently reported alkaline electrolyzers withoutPt-groupmetals(Figure 5fandTableS5,SupportingIn- formation).Thechronopotentiometrytestofﬂower-shapedV:Co- ReS2isconductedatﬁxedcurrentdensitiesof10,20,and100mA cm−2foraminimumof100h,conﬁrmingtheexceptionalstabil- ityoftheV:Co-ReS2||RuO2electrolyzer(Figure 5g). Moreover, we constructed an anion exchange membrane (AEM)waterelectrolyzeroperatingat25–50 °Cin1mKOHsolu- tiontoevaluateourcatalystforindustrialwatersplitting(Figure S28a,b,SupportingInformation).V:Co-ReS2||RuO2AEMwater electrolyzer reached a cell current density of 500 and 1000 mA cm−2byapplyingjust1.78Vcelland1.96Vcell,respectively,across the electrodes at 50 °C( F i g u r e S28c, Supporting Information). Notably,ourAEMwaterelectrolyzersrequiredlowercellvoltages to obtain the desired current density than previously reported 2DTMD-basedAEMwaterelectrolyzersundersimilaroperating conditions (Figure S28d, Supporting Information), demonstrat- ingthesuperiorityofourcatalystforwaterelectrolysis. 3.Conclusion In summary, we introduce a universal platform for dual TM- doped TMD electrocatalysts designed for wide pH HER using oxidizedTifoils.TheuniqueﬂippedDMinCo-ReS2intheSTEM image allows the identiﬁcation of uniformly dispersed V- and Co-doped ReS2. The HER catalytic activity has low overpoten- tials of 31, 83, and 59 mV at a current density of 10 mA cm−2 underacidic,neutral,andalkalineconditions,respectively,with high durability exceeding 70 h in all media at 200 mA cm−2. DFT simulations demonstrate that the dual TM doping system of ReS2enhances hydrogen evolution in high pH media (pH ≥ 7)bysigniﬁcantlyloweringthewaterdissociationbarrier ΔGH2O andachievingthermoneutral ΔGH*.Ultimately,theintimatecou- plingofdualTM-dopedReS2onarobustTiOxplatformenhanced the HER durability for long-term stability. Our strategy does Small2024,20,2308672 ©2023Wiley-VCHGmbH 2308672(7of11) 16136829, 2024, 22, Downloaded from https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/smll.202308672 by Beijing University of Chemistry Technology, Wiley Online Library on [30/03/2026]. See the Terms and Conditions (https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/terms-and-conditions) on Wiley Online Library for rules of use; OA articles are governed by the applicable Creative Commons License
