www.advancedsciencenews.com www.small-journal.com electron-core interaction was described using the projector-augmented wave(PAW)method.[42]TheBrillouinzonewassampledusinga3 ×3×1 k-point mesh, while the electronic states were smeared using the Methfessel −Paxton scheme with a broadening width of 0.1 eV. For den- sity of states (DOS) calculations, a 6 ×6×1k-point mesh was used for Brillouinzoneintegration.Theelectronicwavefunctionswereexpandedin aplanewavebasiswithacutoﬀenergyof400eV,andtheatomicrelaxation was continued until the Hellmann −Feynman forces acting on the atoms werelessthan0.02eVÅ−1.FormodelingH2O,H ─OH,andHadsorption structures, a 4 ×4 supercell of ReS2was employed. Additionally, a 10 × 4 supercell of ReS2was utilized for DM ﬂipping by Co and V doping. In eachsystem,avacuumlayerof13ÅwasaddedontotheReS2surfaceto eliminatepossibleinterlayerinteractions.ThefreeenergyofHadsorption isdeﬁnedas ΔGH*=ΔEH+ΔEZPE-TΔSH,whereΔEHistheHadsorp- tion energy, ΔEZPEis the zero-point energy diﬀerence, Tis room temper- ature,ΔSHis the diﬀerence in entropy, and ΔEZPE-TΔSHis 0.24 eV.[43] ΔGH2O=ΔEH2O+0.43 eV, where ΔEH2Oisthe energy diﬀerence before andafterwatermoleculedissociationonthesurface.[44] SupportingInformation SupportingInformationisavailablefromtheWileyOnlineLibraryorfrom theauthor. Acknowledgements L.A.A. and S.J.K. contributed equally to this work. K.K.K. acknowl- edges support from the Basic Science Research (2020R1A4A3079710, 2022R1A2C2091475) and Next-Generation Intelligence Semiconductor Program(2022M3F3A2A01072215)throughtheNationalResearchFoun- dation of Korea (NRF), which is funded by the Ministry of Science, ICT & Future Planning and the Institute for Basic Science (IBS-R011- D1). Y.-K.H. acknowledges support from the Basic Science Research Program through the National Research Foundation of Korea (NRF), which is funded by the Ministry of Science, ICT & Future Planning (2022R1A2C2008968). Y.H.L. acknowledges support from the Institute for Basic Science (I