Coordination Chemistry Reviews 514 (2024) 215899 17the abundant Ni/NiO heterogeneous interface can significantly strengthen the electrochemically active area. The O 1 s spectrum (Fig. 13h) has the richest concentration of Ni/NiO-cp O vacancies, which can accelerate the adsorption of H2O molecule, and facilitate the proton transport in the electrolyte [168] . Although significant progress has been made for high-performance transition metal based electrocatalysts due to their earth abundance, versatile structure, multi-valence and moderate ΔGH, few of them can compete with Pt-based electrocatalysts. Moreover, transition metals are prone to proceed redox reactions with electrolytes in strong acids, resulting in changes in the composition and function of their original electrocatalytic sites, affecting stability. Therefore, doping, defect en- gineering and complex with conductive substrates are used to regulate the composition, morphological structure of electrocatalyst. This leads to the optimization of density of active sites and thermodynamic hydrogen behaviors on the surface, spiring the development of efficient and stable transition metal based electrocatalysts, which are shown in Table 2. 3.3. Metal-free electrocatalysts Metal-free electrocatalysts are widely used as substitute for metal- based HER electrocatalysts due to their tunable structures, versatile compositions, abundant sources, good conductivity, environmental compatibility and low-cost [19]. Till now, metal-free electrocatalysts especially carbonaceous materials have been popularly engaged and extended to non-carbonaceous materials. Carbonaceous materials such as graphite, diamond and amorphous carbon, carbon allotropes including 0D fullerene and carbon dots, 1D carbon nanotubes, 2D gra- phene and graphdiyne, biomass carbon architectures, and carbon nitride have shown great potentials as the electrocatalysts [169] . Since the discovery of nitrogen doped vertically aligned carbon nanotubes for ORR electrocatalysis, which is superior to Pt without CO deactivation, the interest in carbon based electrocatalysts has been enlightened [170] . Non-carbonaceous metal-free materials including boron nitride and phosphorus-based materials are attracting much more attention because of their excellent charge transfer properties in addition to their large surface areas [171] . 3.3.1. 0D carbon-based electrocatalysts Fullerene-based electrocatalysts. Fullerenes (C60) is a well-known and widely utilized carbon allotrope with a spherical structure composed with sp2-hybridized carbon atoms. C60 has received much attention as an HER electrocatalyst because of its distinct structure, excellent electron-accepting capability, and strong electron-transporting property [172] . C60 with extremely high electrochemical stability shows a low onset potential of ␀0.13 V [173] . Echegoyen et al. [174] suc- cessfully synthesized, characterized and analyzed the electrocatalytic Table 2 Summary of the HER activities of various transition metal based electrocatalysts. Category Electrocatalysts Modification Support Electrolyte (Solution media) η10 (mV) Tafel Slope (mV dec␀1) ΔGH* (eV) Ref TMSs MoS 2 ML Morphology Carbon cloth 0.5 M H2SO4 126 67 —— [114] S-MoS 2@C 136 78 0.52 [113] CoS 2-CF-4 Glassy carbon 121 68 —— [115] CoS x/MoS 2LE Doped 1 M KOH 200 110 —— [116] NiSx/MoS 2LE 180 100 —— [116] Ni-MoS 2 0.5 M H2SO4 240 66.27 —— [118] Co-MoS 2 —— 68.53 —— [118] Fe-MoS 2 —— 93.67 —— [118] Co-Pd-MoS 2 49.3 43.2 ␀0.09 [119] N-Ni 3S2 Ni foam 1 M KOH 155 113 0.036 [122] 1 T-MoS 2 Tuning phase Graphite discs 0.5 M H2SO4 187 43 —— [124] 50 % 1 T MoS 2 Glassy carbon 126 35 —— [127] Se4-MoS 2 Doped/ Tuning phase 108 47 —— [128] TiS2-x/NiS Vacancy-defective Ni foam 0.5 M H2SO4 1 M KOH 134 63 80.9 43.6 0.137 [131] TMPs Ni2P —— Ti foil 0.5 M H2SO4 —— 46 —— [137] CoP —— Glassy carbon 135 90 —— [141] Co2P —— 154 101 —— [141] MoP —— Ti foil 117 50 —— [143] NiMoP Alloy Glassy carbon 1 M KOH 400 163 —— [146] NiMnP 49