ing more defects and active sites as well as speeding up charge transfer [216,228,229] . Zhi et al. [230] demonstrated that the performance of g-C3N4 as HER electrocatalyst Fig. 16.Classic researches for graphitic carbon nitride-based electrocatalysts. a. Triazine and b. tri-s-triazine (heptazine) structures of g-C3N4. c. Synthesis process of CNQDs@G hybrid. d. Bader charge analysis. e. Free energy diagrams for HER. Copyright 2018, ACS. Reproduced with permission from ref [224] C. Wang et al.
