of multicomponent heterostructures is an e ﬀective and prom- ising strategy for enhancing the electrocatalytic performance of electrocatalysts. In this article, the design of multicomponent hetero- structures with a focus on optimizing the ability to balance the adsorption and desorption of intermediates for enhancing theactivity of water electrocatalysis will be highlighted. First of all, achievements relating to multicomponent heterostructure engineering for the hydrogen evolution reaction (HER) areintroduced. Herein, multicomponent heterostructure engineer- ing mainly plays di ﬀerent roles: adjusting the binding energy ofH adsto a suitable value; acting as the “deliverymen ”to facili- tate the transfer of Hads; and introducing a “promoter ”to improve the rate of water dissociation. Then, multicomponent heterostructure engineering for boosting OER performance isillustrated. The design of multicomponent heterostructures plays a role in balancing the adsorption and desorption of partial oxygen species or each oxygen species during the OERprocess. Finally, conclusions and perspectives are presented to reveal the challenges and future directions of multicomponent heterostructure design. The design of multicomponent heterostructures for electrocatalysis Since electrocatalysis is a process that highly depends on the adsorption and desorption of intermediates, the design of multicomponent heterostructures has attracted vast attention for developing highly e ﬃcient electrocatalysts. A large number of explorations and investigations has proved that enhanced electrocatalytic activity can be achieved viabalancing the adsorption and desorption of intermediates using electrocata-lysts. 11In this section, achievements relating to the design of multicomponent heterostructures will be introduced by pre- senting recent studies on water splitting. Multicomponent heterostructure engineering for the HER Hydrogen generation viaelectrocatalysis is an e ﬀective and environmentally friendly process for producing high purity hydrogen energy. The HER is a typical electrocatalytic reaction that obeys Sabatier ’s principle.9According to Sabatier ’s prin- ciple, the exploitation of advanced HER electrocatalysts is determined based on interactions between the intermediate Hadsand electrocatalysts. If the binding energy between Hads and the electrocatalyst is too weak, the adsorption of Hadsis slow and, thus, the overall reaction rate decreases. If it is too strong, the desorption of Hadsbecomes di ﬃcult and the whole reaction rate decreases as well. That is to say, the adsorption energy of Hadsshould be neither too high nor too low. The design of multicomponent heterostructures is a powerful strat-egy for adjusting the adsorption energy of H adsand has shown great results, enhancing the HER activity. For example, Wang et al. have revealed that the HER activity of Pt could be greatly increased upon coupling with black phosphorus (BP).12The formation of Pt –P bonds between Pt and BP lowers the d-bandcenter of Pt, consequently yielding optimal energetics in relation to the binding energy of Hadsduring the HER. Based on this, a BP-activated Pt/graphite composite (designated BPed-Pt/GR) shows a current density of 82.89 mA cm−2at 70 mV, more than 5.6 times that of commercial Pt/C (Fig. 2a –c). As shown in Fig. 2d –f, a MoS 2/Mo 2C multicompo- nent heterostructure was designed viathe carburization of MoS 2.13This hybrid electrocatalyst exhibits outstanding HER performance, with an overpotential of 63 mV to reach 10 mA cm−2and a low Tafel slope of 48 mV dec−1, and excellent stabi- lity in 0.5 M H 2SO4, much better than the corresponding Mo 2C and MoS 2components alone. The high HER activity arises from the formation of a MoS 2/Mo 2C heterostructure with near- zero Gibbs free energy of hydrogen adsorption. Encouraged by density functional theory (DFT) predictions, Mu ’s group incor- porated RuP 2with N,P dual –doped carbon (NPC), producing an optimal Hadsadsorption energy value of 0.233 eV; this not only leads to Pt-like HER activity with a small overpotential, but also superior stability and 100% faradaic yields.14 Recent investigations have shown that the design of multi- component heterostructures for electrocatalysts that disobey Sabatier ’s principle can also show superior HER properties. In these electrocatalysts, di ﬀerent components take charge of diﬀerent HER procedures. A typical system is the combination of noble metals and silicon nanowires, as reported by Shao ’s group (Fig. 2g –i).10For example, in the Rh/Si electrocatalyst, the Rh section is responsible for the adsorption of hydrogen Fig. 2 (a and b) TEM and HRTEM images of BPed-Pt/GR. (c) The free energy of the optimal HER site in each system with di ﬀerent Pt –P content values. Reproduced with permission from ref. 12, copyright: 2019, Wiley-VCH. (d and e) The SEM and HRTEM characterization of MoS 2/Mo 2C hybrid nanosheets; the inset of (e) shows the corresponding lattice fringes of MoS 2.( f )D i ﬀerential Gibbs free energy ΔGdiﬀ(n) and enthalpy ΔEdiﬀ(n) for H adsorption on the fully CH x-modi ﬁed S edge of MoS 2. Reproduced with permission from ref. 13, copyright: 2017, American Chemical Society. (g and h) TEM and HRTEM images of Rh/ SiNW. (i) A schematic representation of the HER reaction mechanism of Rh/SiNW. Reproduced with permission from ref. 10, copyright: 2016,Nature Publishing Group.Frontier Dalton Transactions Dalton Trans. This journal is © The Royal Society of Chemistry 2020 Published on 27 January 2020. Downloaded by Universite Paris Descartes on 2/14/2020 3:10:10 PM. View Article Online 是一种有效且有前景的策略，用于提高电催化剂的电催化性能。 本文将重点介绍多组分异质结构的设计，重点关注优化中 间体吸附和脱附能力以增强水电催化活性的设计。首先，介绍 了与析氢反应（HER）相关的多组分异质结构工程方面的成果。 在此，多组分异质结构工程主要发挥不同作用：将Hads的结合 能调整到合适值；充当“递送员”以促进Hads的转移；引入 “促进剂”以提高水裂解速率。然后，阐述了用于提升析氧反 应（OER）性能的多组分异质结构工程。多组分异质结构的设 计在OER过程中平衡部分氧物种或每种氧物种的吸附和脱附发 挥着作用。最后，提出了结论和展望，以揭示多组分异质结构 设计的挑战和未来方向。 多组分异质结构的设计用于电催化 由于电催化是一个高度依赖于中间体的吸附和解吸的过程，多 组分异质结构的设计已吸引了大量关注，用于开发高效电催化 剂。大量探索和研究证明，通过使用电催化剂平衡中间体的吸 附和解吸，可以实现增强的电催化活性。11在本节中，将通过 介绍水分解的最新研究，来介绍与多组分异质结构设计相关的 研究成果。 用于析氢反应的多组分异质结构工程 通过电催化制氢是一种有效且环保的高纯度氢能源生产过程。析氢反应（ HER）是一种典型的电催化反应，遵循萨巴蒂尔原理。9根据萨巴蒂尔原理， 先进HER电催化剂的开发是基于中间体Hads与电催化剂之间的相互作用。如果 Hads与电催化剂之间的结合能太弱，Hads的吸附会缓慢，从而导致整体反应速 率降低。如果结合能太强，Hads的脱附会变得困难，整体反应速率同样会降低。 也就是说，Hads的吸附能既不能太高也不能太低。多组分异质结构的设计是调 节Hads吸附能的一种强大策略，已取得显著成果，增强了HER活性。例如，王 等人发现，将铂（Pt）与黑磷（BP）耦合后，其HER活性会显著提高。12Pt 与BP之间形成的Pt–P键降低了Pt的d带中心，从而在HER过程中与H9的结合 能关系上产生了最佳能效。基于这一点，BP活化的Pt/石墨复合材料（简称 BPed‑Pt/GR）在70mV时的电流密度为82.89mAcmads，是商业Pt/C（图 2a–c）的5.6倍以上。如图2d–f所示，通过MoSads的碳化设计了MoSads/Mo adsC多组分异质结构。ads这种混合电催化剂表现出优异的HER性能，在达到 10mAcmads时过电位为63mV，塔菲尔斜率为48mVdec12，在0.5M HSO中的稳定性远优于相应的MoC和MoS单一组分。这种高HER活性源于 MoS/MoC异质结构的形成，其氢吸附的吉布斯自由能接近于零。受密度泛函 理论（DFT）预测的鼓舞，Mu等人将RuP与N,P双掺杂碳（NPC）结合，产生 了0.233eV的最佳H吸附能值；这不仅带来了Pt样的HER活性（过电位小）， 还实现了优异的稳定性和100%的法拉第产率。铂的中心，从而在析氢反应过程中与Hads的结合能产生最佳能 学关系。基于此，BP活化铂/石墨复合材料（记为 BPed‑Pt/GR）在70mV时展现出82.89mAcm−2的电流密度， 是商业Pt/C的5.6倍以上（图2a–c）。如图2d–f所示，通过 MoS2的碳化设计了一种MoS2/Mo2C多组分异质结构。该混合 电催化剂表现出优异的析氢性能，在达到10mAcm−2时过电 位为63mV，塔菲尔斜率为48mVdec−1，并且在0.5MH2 SO4,中具有优异的稳定性，远优于单独的Mo2C和MoS2组分。 其高析氢活性源于MoS2/Mo2C异质结构的形成，该结构具有近 于零的氢吸附吉布斯自由能。受密度泛函理论（DFT）预测的 鼓舞，Mu团队将RuP2与N,P双掺杂碳（NPC）结合，获得了 0.233eV的最优Hads吸附能；这不仅导致了具有小过电位的 Pt样析氢活性，还实现了优异的稳定性和100%的法拉第产率14。 近期研究表明，设计违背萨巴蒂尔原理的多组分异质结电催化剂 也能表现出优异的析氢反应（HER）性能。在这些电催化剂中，不同 组分负责不同的HER过程。一个典型的体系是贵金属与硅纳米线的组 合，如Shao研究组报道的那样（图2g–i）。10例如，在Rh/Si电催化 剂中，Rh部分负责吸附氢离子，而Si部分则为吸附的氢原子和氢离子 反应生成分子氢提供场所。异质结在此处的角色是将吸附的氢原子从 Rh转移到Si。因此，Rh/Si的HER活性远优于单独的Rh纳米颗粒或 Si纳米线。 图2(a和b)BPed‑Pt/GR的TEM和HRTEM图像。(c)每个系统中不同Pt‑P 含量值下最优析氢位点的自由能。经参考文献12许可转载，版权：2019， Wiley‑VCH。(d和e)MoS2/Mo2C杂化纳米片的SEM和HRTEM表征；(e) 的插图显示了相应的MoS2晶格条纹。(f)H在完全CHx‑修饰的S边缘上吸附 的微分吉布斯自由能ΔGdiﬀ(n)和焓ΔEdiﬀ(n)。经参考文献13许可转载，版 权：2017，美国化学会。(g和h)Rh/SiNW的TEM和HRTEM图像。(i) Rh/SiNW析氢反应机理的示意图。经参考文献10许可转载，版权：2016， 自然出版集团。前沿 Dalton交易 DaltonTrans. 本期刊受英国皇家化学学会版权保护，2020年 Published on 27 January 2020. Downloaded byUniversite Paris Descartes on2/14/2020 3:10:10 PM. 在线查看文章
