ions, and the Si section provides a place for the reaction of adsorbed H atoms and hydrogen ions to produce molecular hydrogen. The role of the heterostructure here is to transferthe adsorbed H atoms from Rh to Si. Consequently, the HER activity of Rh/Si is much better than Rh nanoparticles or Si nanowires alone. In general, two pathways are widely accepted as occurring during the HER: the Volmer –Heyrovsky and Volmer –Tafel pathways. 15The Heyrovsky and Volmer steps have di ﬀerent courses in acidic and basic solution. Compared with the acidic HER, the alkaline HER is more complicated; the rate of water dissociation influences the overall HER kinetics. Therefore, thecleavage of O –H bonds in water is vital. 16Through the design of multicomponent heterostructures, a “promoter ”, which can accelerate the rate of water dissociation, can be introducedinto an electrocatalyst and, thus, the HER activity in alkaline media can be improved. Zhang et al. synthesized a novel Ni (OH) 2/MoS 2@CC electrocatalyst with greatly enhanced alkaline HER activity (Fig. 3a –e).17This improved performance is due to the formation of a Ni(OH) 2/MoS 2multicomponent hetero- structure, in which Ni(OH) 2acts as a water cleavage promoter, while MoS 2serves as the location for intermediate Hadsadsorp- tion and desorption. As shown in Fig. 3f –i, Fu et al. investi- gated the controllable surface modification of V 8C7/monolayer graphene (G) heterostructures using nitrogen.18The optimized N0.08-G/V 8C7displays exceptional alkaline HER abilities due totwo factors. On one hand, owing to the electronic coupling of N and V, the V sites can e ﬀectively decrease the kinetic energy barrier for water adsorption and dissociation. On the otherhand, the accumulation of electrons on graphene allows it to provide sites for H adsadsorption and subsequent desorption. Based on composition-segregated Pt –Ni nanowires, our group designed a series of metal/metal oxide (sulfide) multi- component heterostructures for alkaline HER electrocata- lysts.19,20A new class of Pt –Ni NWs/C-air with Pt –Ni/NiO x multicomponent heterostructures, which show obviously enhanced HER activity compared with commercial Pt/C and Pt–Ni nanowires, were designed viathe simple thermal treat- ment of composition-segregated Pt –Ni nanowires in air.19In our latest work, Pt –Ni/NiS xNWs with Pt –Ni/NiS xmulticompo- nent heterostructures were obtained viathe sulphur treatment of composition-segregated Pt –Ni NWs (Fig. 3j –l).20Pt3Ni2 NWs-S/C can reach a current density of 37.2 mA cm−2at 70 mV, over 9.7 times higher than commercial Pt/C at pH 14.The enhanced HER activity in alkaline media arises from a synergistic e ﬀect involving Pt –Ni/NiS xor Pt –Ni/NiO xmulticom- ponent heterostructures. During the process of the HER inalkaline media, water cleavage can be accelerated viaNiS xor NiO x. Then, the intermediates Hadsand OH−can be e ﬀectively separated with the cooperation of Ni2+and Pt. Therefore, the HER performance in alkaline media is largely enhanced. In brief, the design of multicomponent heterostructures is an eﬀective strategy for boosting the HER activity in three main respects: optimizing the binding energy of Hads; acting as“deliverymen ”that can facilitate the transfer of Hads; and introducing a “promoter ”that can accelerate the rate of water dissociation. Multicomponent heterostructure engineering for the OER The OER, with its four-electron process, is a relatively compli- cated reaction involving various intermediates, such as HO*, O*, and HOO*, in which * represents an electrocatalyst site.21 Normally, the widely accepted OER mechanisms in acidic and alkaline media are represented as follows. Under acidic conditions: H2Oþ/C3 $ HO/C3þHþþe/C0 HO/C3$ O/C3þHþþe/C0 O/C3þH2O$HOO/C3þHþþe/C0 HOO/C3$ O2þ/C3þ Hþþe/C0: Under alkaline conditions: OH/C0þ/C3 $ HO/C3þe/C0 HO/C3þOH/C0$O/C3þH2Oþe/C0 O/C3þOH/C0$HOO/C3þe/C0 HOO/C3þOH/C0$O2þH2Oþe/C0 Previous theoretical and experimental investigations have demonstrated that the binding energies of these intermediates Fig. 3 (a–c) SEM and TEM images of Ni(OH) 2/MoS 2@CC. (d) A sche- matic illustration of water activation, H* intermediate formation, and thehydrogen generation processes on a MoS 2catalyst and Ni(OH) 2/MoS 2 hybrid catalyst. (e) The corresponding free energy diagram for the HERon MoS 2edges and at the Ni(OH) 2/MoS 2interface. Reproduced with permission from ref. 17, copyright: 2017, Elsevier. (f and g) TEM and HAADF-STEM images of N 0.08-G/V 8C7. (h and i) Energy diagrams and simpli ﬁed surface structures of the various reaction species during the Volmer step for the alkaline HER on N 0.08-G/V 8C7and G/V 8C7surfaces, and during the Heyrovsky step on N 0.08-G/V 8C7. Reproduced with per- mission from ref. 18, copyright: 2019, Wiley-VCH. ( j) A HRTEM image of Pt3Ni3NWs-S. The inset shows the corresponding TEM image. (k) A reaction energy diagram showing water dissociation on the Pt(111) surface (black) and NiS(100) surface (red). (l) The free-energy barriers for the HER on the Pt(111) surface (black), Pt 3Ni(111) surface (red and blue) and NiS(100) surface (green), respectively. Reproduced with permission from ref. 20, copyright: 2017, Nature Publishing Group.Dalton Transactions Frontier This journal is © The Royal Society of Chemistry 2020 Dalton Trans. Published on 27 January 2020. Downloaded by Universite Paris Descartes on 2/14/2020 3:10:10 PM. View Article Online 离子，而Si部分则为吸附的氢原子和氢离子反应生成分子氢提 供场所。异质结在此处的角色是将吸附的氢原子从Rh转移到 Si。因此，Rh/Si的HER活性远优于单独的Rh纳米颗粒或Si纳 米线。 通常认为，在析氢反应（HER）过程中存在两种主要途径： Volmer–Heyrovsky途径和Volmer–Tafel途径.15 Heyrovsky步骤和Volmer步骤在酸性和碱性溶液中的反应过 程不同。与酸性HER相比，碱性HER更为复杂；水的解离速率 会影响整体HER动力学。因此，水分子中O–H键的断裂至关重 要.16通过设计多组分异质结构，可以将一种“促进剂”引入电 催化剂中，该促进剂能够加速水的解离，从而提高碱性介质中 的HER活性。张等人合成了一种新型Ni(OH)2/MoS2@CC电催 化剂，其碱性HER活性显著增强（图3a–e）.17这种性能的提 升是由于形成了Ni(OH)2/MoS2多组分异质结构，其中 Ni(OH)2作为水解离促进剂，而MoS2则作为中间体Hads吸附 和解吸的位点。如图3f–i所示，付等人利用氮对V8C7/单层石墨 烯（G）异质结构的可控表面改性进行了研究.18优化的N0.08‑ G/V8C7表现出优异的碱性HER能力，这是由于两个因素。一方面，由于N和V之间的电子耦合，V位点可以有 效降低水吸附和解离的动力学能垒。另一方面，石墨烯上的电 子积累使其能够提供Hads吸附和后续解吸的位点。 基于成分分离的Pt‑Ni纳米线，我们的团队设计了一系列金 属/金属氧化物（硫化物）多组分异质结构，用于碱性析氢反应 （HER）电催化剂。19,20我们设计了一种新型Pt‑NiN Ws/C空气材料，其中包含Pt‑Ni/NiOx多组分异质结构，其 HER活性明显优于商业Pt/C和Pt‑Ni纳米线，这是通过在空气 中对成分分离的Pt‑Ni纳米线进行简单的热处理获得的。19在我 们的最新工作中，通过成分分离的Pt‑NiNWs的硫处理获得了 Pt‑Ni/NiSxNWs与Pt‑Ni/NiSx多组分异质结构（图3j‑l）。 20Pt3Ni2NWs‑S/C在70mV时可以达到37.2mAcm−2的电流 密度，比pH14条件下的商业Pt/C高9.7倍以上。碱性介质中增 强的HER活性源于Pt‑Ni/NiSx或Pt‑Ni/NiOx多组分异质结构 的协同效应。在碱性介质中HER的过程中，水裂解可以通过 NiSx或NiOx加速。然后，在Ni2+和Pt的协同作用下，中间体 Hads和OH−可以被有效分离。因此，碱性介质中的HER性能 得到显著增强。 简而言之，多组分异质结构的设计是提高析氢反应（ HER）活性的有效策略，主要体现在以下三个方面：优化Hads 的结合能；充当“递送者”，促进Hads的转移；引入“促进剂”， 加速水分子解离的速率。 MulticomponentheterostructureengineeringfortheOER 析氧反应（OER）具有四电子过程，是一种相对复杂的反应， 涉及多种中间体，如HO*、O*和HOO*（*代表电催化剂位点）。 21通常，在酸性和碱性介质中广泛接受的OER机理表示如下。 在酸性条件下： H2Oþ/C3$HO/C3þHþþe/C0 HO/C3$O/C3þHþþe/C0 O/C3þH2O$HOO/C3þHþþe/C0 HOO/C3$O2þ/C3þHþþe/C0: 在碱性条件下： OH/C0þ/C3$HO/C3þe/C0 HO/C3þOH/C0$O/C3þH2Oþe/C0 O/C3þOH/C0$HOO/C3þe/C0 HOO/C3þOH/C0$O2þH2Oþe/C0 以往的理论和实验研究已经证明，这些中间体的结合能 图3(a–c)Ni(OH)2/MoS2@CC的SEM和TEM图像。(d)MoS2催化剂和 Ni(OH)2/MoS2杂化催化剂上水活化、H*中间体形成及氢气生成过程的示意 图。(e)MoS2边缘和Ni(OH)2/MoS2界面处析氢反应(HER)的对应自由能 图。经参考文献17许可转载，版权：2017，Elsevier。(f和g)N0.08‑G/V8C7 的TEM和HAADF‑STEM图像。(h和i)N0.08‑G/V8C7和G/V8C7表面碱性 HER过程中Volmer步骤的各种反应物种的能量图和简化表面结构，以及 N0.08‑G/V8C7表面Heyrovsky步骤的能量图。经参考文献18许可转载，版权： 2019，Wiley‑VCH。(j)Pt3Ni3NWs‑S的HRTEM图像。插图显示相应的 TEM图像。(k)显示水在Pt(111)表面(黑色)和NiS(100)表面(红色)上解离的 反应能图。(l)Pt(111)表面(黑色)、Pt3Ni(111)表面(红色和蓝色)和 NiS(100)表面(绿色)上析氢反应(HER)的自由能势垒。经参考文献20许可转 载，版权：2017，NaturePublishingGroup。Dalton交易 前沿 本期刊受英国皇家化学学会©版权保护2020 Dalton交易 Published on 27 January 2020. Downloaded byUniversite Paris Descartes on2/14/2020 3:10:10 PM. 在线查看文章
