on the electrocatalysts have a great influence on the OER activity.22,23Based on this perspective, a balance between the adsorption and desorption of intermediates on electrocatalystsis a basis for an excellent OER catalyst; this can be e ﬀectively modified viathe design of multicomponent heterostructures. Zhao et al. prepared a novel Au nanocluster/CoSe 2electroca- talyst for enhancing the OER properties.24The nanocluster/ CoSe 2multicomponent heterostructure was formed viathe vig- orous stirring of Au nanoclusters and CoSe 2in dichloro- methane (Fig. 4a –c). DFT calculations reveal that the construc- tion of the Au/CoSe 2multicomponent heterostructure favors the formation of HOO* and the desorption of O 2. Nowadays, transition metal layered double hydroxides (LDHs) have attracted much attention due to their superior OER activities. As illustrated in Fig. 4d and e, Gao et al. designed a NiO/NiFe multicomponent heterostructure for a NiO/NiFe LDH compo- site, which exhibits superior OER activity with a low potential of about 205 mV at 30 mA cm−2.25Cooperation between NiO nanoparticles and NiFe LDH nanosheets provides sites for adjusting the adsorption energy of each intermediate indepen- dently and results in enhanced performance (Fig. 4f). Li et al. anchored Ru single atoms on CoFe LDHs viaa simple wetchemical method.26The boosting of the OER activity arises due to the role of the single atom noble metal/LDH multicom- ponent heterostructure, which not only optimizes the adsorp-tion of HOO* but also avoids the oxidation of Ru. Our group also carried out some research into enhancing the OER activity viathe design of multicomponent hetero- structures. For instance, a highly distributed iridium-based alloy supported on carbon was achieved viaa wet-chemical method. The OER activity in acid was improved due to theclose heterostructure formed between the iridium-based alloy and carbon. 27Besides, a series of Ni(OH) 2–CeO 2catalysts sup- ported on carbon paper (Ni xCey@CP) with close Ni(OH) 2–CeO 2 multicomponent heterostructures were constructed viaa solvo- thermal method (Fig. 4g –j).28The test results showed out- standing activity and stability for the OER with a low overpo-tential and a small Tafel slope. The enhanced performance may be attributed to the Ni(OH) 2–CeO 2multicomponent heterostructure, which modulates the binding strengthbetween intermediates and the electrocatalyst. In general, by balancing the adsorption and desorption of partial intermediates or each intermediate through the designof multicomponent heterostructures during the OER process, the whole reaction rate can be greatly increased. Conclusions and Perspectives In this article, the success of using multicomponent hetero-structure engineering to obtain highly e ﬃcient electrocatalysts is highlighted by illustrating the di ﬀerent roles that multicom- ponent heterostructures play in the HER and OER. The posi- tive eﬀects of multicomponent heterostructures for enhancing the electrocatalytic activity come from their great ability tobalance the adsorption and desorption of intermediates. Although great achievements have been made, several perspec- tives should still be taken into consideration. The first point that needs to be considered is the stability of the multicomponent heterostructures. As we know, most electrocatalytic reactions take place at extremely negative orpositive potentials. These extreme conditions will unavoidably cause partial or even wholescale changes to electrocatalysts and, thus, the corresponding multicomponent hetero-structures will also change. Whether the changed multicompo- nent heterostructures are beneficial for enhancing the electro- catalytic activity or not should be further studied. Recently,several typical strategies have been adopted to improve the stability of multicomponent heterostructures, such as surface modification, doping, thermal treatment, in situ growth, and support e ﬀects. However, improving the stability of multicom- ponent heterostructures is still an area that needs further study. Secondly, the design of multicomponent heterostructures possesses unique superiority for the adjustment of electrocata- lysis selectivity. Unlike the above mentioned electrocatalyticreactions, the electrochemical reduction of carbon dioxide is a kind of reaction with a wide range of products, such as carbon Fig. 4 (a and b) HAADF-STEM images of a Au 25/CoSe 2composite at diﬀerent magni ﬁcations. (c) The proposed mechanism for the oxygen evolution reaction in the presence of a gold atom on the CoSe 2catalyst surface. Reproduced with permission from ref. 24, copyright: 2017,American Chemical Society. (d and e) TEM and HRTEM images of NiO/ NiFe LDH; the inset of (e) shows the corresponding low magni ﬁcation TEM image. (f) A 2D image showing the dynamic tridimensional adsorp-tion of intermediates at the NiO/LDH intersection and traditional single site adsorption on a planar surface. Reproduced with permission from ref. 25, copyright: 2019, Wiley-VCH. (g –i) SEM and HRTEM images of Ni 4Ce1@CP. ( j) Schematic diagrams showing the OER processes on Ni@CP and Ni 4Ce1@CP with close Ni(OH) 2–CeO 2interfaces. Reproduced with permission from ref. 28, copyright: 2018, American Chemical Society.Frontier Dalton Transactions Dalton Trans. This journal is © The Royal Society of Chemistry 2020 Published on 27 January 2020. Downloaded by Universite Paris Descartes on 2/14/2020 3:10:10 PM. View Article Online 对电催化剂有重大影响，22,23基于这一观点，电催化剂上中间 体的吸附和脱附之间的平衡是优异的析氧反应催化剂的基础； 这可以通过多组分异质结构的设计来有效调节。 赵等人制备了一种新型Au纳米簇/CoSe2电催化剂，用于 增强析氧反应（OER）性能.24该纳米簇/CoSe2多组分异质结 构是通过Au纳米簇和CoSe2在二氯甲烷中的剧烈搅拌形成的 （图4a–c）.DFT计算表明，Au/CoSe2多组分异质结构的构 建有利于HOO*的形成和O2的脱附.如今，过渡金属层状双氢氧 化物（LDHs）因其优异的OER活性而备受关注.如图4d和e所 示，高等人设计了一种NiO/NiFe多组分异质结构，用于 NiO/NiFeLDH复合物，该复合物在30mAcm−2下具有约 205mV的低电位.25NiO纳米颗粒和NiFeLDH纳米片之间的 协同作用为独立调节每个中间体的吸附能提供了位点，从而提 高了性能（图4f）.李等人通过简单的湿化学方法将Ru单原子锚 定在CoFeLDHs上该OER活性的提升是由于单原子贵金属/LDH多组分异质结构 的作用，它不仅优化了HOO*的吸附，还避免了Ru的氧化.26 我们的团队还通过多组分异质结构的设计研究了提高析氧 反应（OER）活性的方法。例如，通过湿化学方法实现了在碳 上负载的高分散度铱基合金。由于铱基合金与碳之间形成的紧 密异质结构，酸性条件下的OER活性得到了提高。27此外，通 过溶剂热法构建了一系列负载在碳纸上的Ni(OH)2–CeO2催化 剂（NixCey@CP），具有紧密的Ni(OH)2–CeO2多组分异质结 构（图4g–j）。28测试结果表明，该OER催化剂具有低过电位 和小的塔菲尔斜率，表现出优异的活性和稳定性。性能的提升 可能归因于Ni(OH)2–CeO2多组分异质结构，它调节了中间体 与电催化剂之间的结合强度。 通常情况下，通过在析氧反应过程中，通过多组分异质结 构的设计来平衡部分中间体或每个中间体的吸附和解吸，可以 使整个反应速率大幅提高。 结论与展望 本文通过阐述多组分异质结构在析氢反应和析氧反应中发挥的 不同作用，突出了利用多组分异质结构工程获得高效电催化剂 的成功。多组分异质结构增强电催化活性的积极作用源于它们 平衡中间体吸附和解吸的强大能力。尽管已取得巨大成就，但 仍需考虑几个方面。 需要考虑的第一点是多组分异质结构的稳定性。众所周知， 大多数电催化反应发生在极负或极正的电位下。这些极端条件 不可避免地会导致电催化剂部分甚至整体发生变化，因此相应 的多组分异质结构也会发生变化。改变后的多组分异质结构是 否有利于增强电催化活性，需要进一步研究。最近，人们已采 用几种典型策略来提高多组分异质结构的稳定性，如表面改性、 掺杂、热处理、原位生长和载体效应。然而，提高多组分异质 结构的稳定性仍是一个需要进一步研究的领域。 其次，多组分异质结构的设计在调整电催化选择性方面具有独特 的优势。与上述电催化反应不同，二氧化碳的电化学还原是一种产物 范围很广的反应，例如碳氧化物、甲酸、乙醇等。合理地调节反应中 间体的吸附和脱附，以实现对目标产物的选择性，是多组分异质结构 设计相关的一个重要挑战。 图4(a和b)不同放大倍数下Au25/CoSe2复合材料的HAADF‑STEM图像。 (c)在CoSe2催化剂表面存在金原子时，析氧反应的提出机理。经参考文献 24授权转载，版权：2017，美国化学会。(d和e)NiO/NiFeLDH的TEM和 HRTEM图像；(e)的插入图为相应的低倍TEM图像。(f)2D图像显示 NiO/LDH交点处中间体的动态三维吸附和传统平面上的单位点吸附。经参 考文献25授权转载，版权：2019，Wiley‑VCH。(g–i)Ni4Ce1@CP的S EM和HRTEM图像。(j)Ni@CP和Ni4Ce1@CP上析氧反应过程的示意图， 具有紧密Ni(OH)2–CeO2界面。经参考文献28授权转载，版权：2018， 美国化学会。前沿 Dalton交易 DaltonTrans. 本期刊受英国皇家化学学会©版权保护2020 Published on 27 January 2020. Downloaded byUniversite Paris Descartes on2/14/2020 3:10:10 PM. 在线查看文章
